{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.751681+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0415e9d7a19b99caeed75b0de45d4827043c726dfaf2c96868190e9591d8024e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:weak_sol_SDE of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $s\in [0,T)$ and \textcolor{black}{$\nu\in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$}. A (weak) solution to SDE$(b,\sigma;s,\textcolor{black}{\nu})$ 
