{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.037274+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_049a49abca4b3617de1796c45ddfc90df1c49c9a5bc00a8825b9d1b285be5e3d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:dichotomy of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] Fix $C_\star>C_{\mathrm{GTD}}$ and $\kappa\ge2C_\star$. Let $h,\gamma>0$ satisfy $h<2/\sqrt\kappa$, and let $s$, $\beta$, and $q_\kappa$ be defined as above. Then at least one of the following two cases holds.

