{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.988483+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_04ed228deb693f79798768102c7ba33be5cbdbcf7c5ce80c05b167a01543bd7c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2609.03386, 'Twisted Gradient Flow Approach to Vegetation-Rainfall-Bushfire Interactions Model'] For each pair $(\tilde{z},\tilde{g}) \in W^{1,2}(0,T;L^2(\Omega)) \times L^2(0,T;L^2(\Omega))$ we consider the following Cauchy problem 
$\text{(TGF)}{}_{\text{{\tiny $\delta,\!\nu$}}}$:=\{(\ref{Equation-2-35})--(\ref{Equation-2-37})\} of a twisted gradient flow with a forcing term on the time-dependent 
twisted spaces $\{L^2(\delta,\bar{z}(t))\,;\,0 \le t \le T\}$:

\begin{gather}

v'(t)+v^*(t)=\tilde{g}(t) \quad \text{in} \quad L^2(\delta,\tilde{z}(t)),\quad \text{a.e.}~t \in (0,T),\\

v^*(t) \in \partial_{\text{{\tiny $\delta,\!\tilde{z}(t)$}}} \Phi_\nu (v(t)),\quad \text{a.e.}~t \in (0,T),\\

v(0)=v_0 \quad \text{in} \quad L^2(\Omega),
