{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.645133+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ad0f3e9ba5e4df534a4e5f6fb65f63ace8cf191ad307044e1bdcff377621181","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm ES-XOR of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] {spin-perc-height}}, {[DRC-1]}]
    Let $D$ be a Jordan domain with discrete domain approximation $D_\delta\subset \delta \mathbb Z^2$. The XOR-Ising model $\tau_\delta$ with free/free boundary conditions in $D_\delta$ can be written as 
    \begin{align*}
        \tau_\delta = \sum_{k=1}^{N} \xi_{k}^\delta \mu_{k}^\delta,
    \end{align*}
    where $(\mu_k^\delta)_{k=1}^N$ is a collection of measures with pairwise disjoint supports $(C_k^\delta)_{k=1}^N$, and $(\xi_k)_{k=1}^N$ are i.i.d. symmetric signs. 

    \noindent The same statement holds under $+/+$ boundary conditions by adding a symmetry-breaking (positive) measure $\mu_0^\delta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.023593+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b209e77216d14ad39b1d09ea15c66fc1fe91ad2261696e130d554ce23f84353","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 8 of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] Let $M$ be a compact connected smooth manifold without boundary, $H$ a Tonelli Hamiltonian on $M$, $\phi\in\SCL(M)$, and $u$ the viscosity solution of \eqref{eq:HJephi pre}. If $x\in\reg(\phi,H)$ and $t\in(0,\tau_{\phi,H}(x)]$ for $\tau_{\phi,H}(x)<+\infty$, or $t\in(0,+\infty)$ for $\tau_{\phi,H}(x)=+\infty$, then there exists a unique $(u,H)$-calibrated curve $\gamma:[0,t]\to M$ with $\gamma(0)=x$, and it is given by
	\begin{align*}
		\gamma(s)=\pi\circ\Phi^s_H(x,D\phi(x)),\qquad \forall s\in[0,t],
	\end{align*}
	where $\pi:T^*M\to M$ is the canonical projection and $\Phi^s_H$ is the Hamiltonian flow of $H$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.551346+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b46a8caa9590e73216d45c53f104380b8d174617253ab07c75e1cf6ed801a99","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2604.01978, 'Homogenized Transformers'] Under Assumption \ref{ass:high_order_short}, 
