{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:02.063585+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0bc16def9b82254c2a3a9864afeb003f8f98a3eabcf68187a4688a437ab1e3da","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop single_tree_size of arXiv:2601.00119, 'The largest common subtree of two random trees'] Let $\tau$ be a Bienaymé tree with offspring distribution $\mu$. Let $\mathrm{h}$ be the largest common divisor of the support of $\mu$, and let $\mathrm{M}$ be the set of integers $m$ such that $\mathbf{P}(\#\tau=m)>0$. Then, there exists a constant $c> 0$ that only depends on $\sigma^2$ such that
   \begin{align*}
   \lim_{\substack{m\to\infty \\ m\in \mathrm{M}}} m^{3/2}\mathbf{P}(\#\tau=m)&=\mathrm{h}c,\\
   \quad \lim_{m\to\infty}m^{1/2}\mathbf{P}(\#\tau\geq m)&= 2c.
   \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.752111+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0bea5acc1415760d42b4797a2c82e30e770bba1c5fe27b504f4d06f18751e677","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:sol_lin_fp of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $s\in [0,T)$ and $\nu\in \mathcal{M}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. A measurable flow ${\boldsymbol\mu}:[s,T)\to \mathcal{M}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ is a (weak) solution to FP$(b,\sigma;s,\nu)$ if
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} \varphi(y) {\boldsymbol\mu}_t (d y)    = \int_{\mathbb{R}^d} \varphi(y) \nu (d y) + \int_{s}^{t} \int_{\mathbb{R}^d}  \Big[\big\langle b(r , y) , \nabla \varphi(y)\big\rangle + \frac{1}{2} \text{tr}\big( \sigma\sigma^\top(r , y ) \nabla^2 \varphi(y) \big)   \Big]  {\boldsymbol\mu}_r (d y) d r, \qquad t\in [s,T),

\end{equation}

for any $\varphi\in C^{\infty}_0(\mathbb{R}^d)$. 

Furthermore, if ${\boldsymbol\mu}_t$ is absolutely continuous with respect to the Lebesgue measure, namely
\begin{equation}
{\boldsymbol\mu}_t (d x) = v_t(x) d x, \qquad t\in [s,T), 
\end{equation}
then the density flow $v:[s,T)\to L^{1}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ will be called a density solution to FP$(b,\sigma;\nu)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.169597+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0bf56791f7e64bad49615b68af5ccd943843604cc71005a7a22a4f55778bf3f2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] Let $p\geq 1$ and $(u, F)$ be any bounded weak solution of \eqref{eq:PDE}.
