\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.651423+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c4c01a09dc9de1a4da9cb1b664dff8dada722c3a742bf88ae3cd3b14fc92069","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 4 (Prior) of arXiv:2605.07050, 'Universality of the fluctuations of the free energy in generalized Sherrington--Kirkpatric'] For a random variable $\bsx = (x_1, \dots, x_N) \in \R^N$ whose distribution is given by a prior $\caX$, we assume that for $i=1, 2, \dots, N$, 
\begin{itemize}
\item The entries $x_i$'s are i.i.d. and the distribution of $\sqrt{N} x_i$ does not depend on $N$.
\item The entries $x_i$'s are symmetric (about $0$) and their variances are normalized so that $\E[x_i^2] = N^{-1}$.
\item for any integer $s>2$, there exists a constant $C^x_s$ such that $\E[|\sqrt{N} x_i|^s] \leq C^x_s$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.877459+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0c4fe30cb4df2df2e2ee85d84647caea6fc26cef9c3b61ba51c8db05bbb53182","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop multgain1 of arXiv:2608.27939, 'Entropy and domination for quasi-Hitchin representations'] Let $\gamma$ be a closed curve on $S$ with $m$ pairwise-disjoint segments, each having the coarse itinerary (equation eq:strict-pattern of the paper). Let $A, A_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_n(\mathbb{C})$ be the determinant-one lifts of $\rho(\gamma), \rho_0(\gamma)$ respectively. Then we have 
