{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.242498+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_15407108d8e6830a2b6488eb32988b0902cfe39c0cc535f33f1be3b259e88ef2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm main of arXiv:2608.30048, 'Counterexamples for generalizations of the non-elliptic Schr\"{o}dinger maximal operator'] Let $n,k\geq 2$. Let $P\in \mathbb{R}[X_1,...,X_n]$ be a polynomial of degree $k$ with leading form 
  \begin{align}
        P_k=
        Q_k+X_1Q_{k-1}+X_1^dQ_{k-d}+X_1^{d+1}Q_{k-(d+1)}+\cdots +X_1^kQ_0,
    \end{align}
    where $2\leq d \leq k$ and $Q_{k-i}\in \mathbb{R}[X_2,...,X_n]$ is a form of degree $k-i$ for all $i=0,1,d,...,k$. Assume $Q_{k-1}$ is not identically zero. Define $s_d=(d-1)/2d$ for $2\leq d \leq k$ and $s_\infty=1/2$.
Suppose there exists a constant $C_s$ such that
    \begin{align}
        \|\sup_{0<t<1}|T_t^Pf|\|_{L^1(B_n(0,1))} \leq C_s \|f\|_{H^s(\mathbb{R}^n)}, \quad \text{for all } f\in H^s(\mathbb{R}^n).
    \end{align}
Then $s\geq s_\infty$ if $Q_{k-i}$ is identically zero for all $d\leq i \leq k$, and otherwise $s\geq s_d$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.695249+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1556a545a579b21bbd7a0a80e0fb5f67139c05615c6ea4a482feaf3de4707ccc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:layer-cake of arXiv:2609.00645, 'Global persistence of nearly radial concentrated vortices in a bounded domain'] Let $f\in L^\infty(\mathbb R^2)$ be nonnegative and compactly supported. Then
