{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:29.000863+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_17926d62c648c4e3e00ec8007005e71f3e72845ff8ab54dc95a24a250eca8976","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop CM UT UB of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] For all $r \in (0, e^{-1} \wedge r_*)$, $t \in (0, \infty)$, and $\lambda \in (0, \infty)$, 
