{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.044174+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_198c2ca3171975ed5b82c64e87cc8c2935246dfb51ce59694baaedaa39a7b286","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:HB of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] Let $(X_k,V_k)_{k\ge0}$ be the OBABO chain (equation eq:obabo1 of the paper)-(equation eq:obabo5 of the paper). Let $\xi_0^{(2)}$ be a $\mathcal N(0,\mathrm{Id}_d)$ variable independent of the pairs $(\xi_k^{(1)},\xi_k^{(2)})_{k\ge1}$ driving the chain. Alternatively, let $\xi_0^{(2)}$ be the zero vector. Define the auxiliary variable $X_{-1}$ by
\begin{equation}
 V_0=r\left(\frac{X_0-X_{-1}}h-\frac h2\nabla U(X_0)\right)
      +\sigma\xi_0^{(2)}.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 X_{k+1}=X_k+\beta(X_k-X_{k-1})
 -s\nabla U(X_k)+\zeta_{k+1},
 \qquad
 s=\frac{h^2}{2}(1+\beta),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
 \zeta_{k+1}=h\sigma\bigl(r\xi_k^{(2)}+\xi_{k+1}^{(1)}\bigr).
\end{equation}
Distinct $\zeta_k$ depend on disjoint noises and are therefore
independent centered Gaussians. If
$\xi_0^{(2)}\sim\mathcal N(0,\mathrm{Id}_d)$, they are identically distributed
with covariance
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E[\zeta_k\zeta_k^\top]
 =h^2(1-\beta^2)\mathrm{Id}_d.
\end{equation}
If $\xi_0^{(2)}=0$, then
\[
 \zeta_1=h\sigma\xi_1^{(1)},\qquad
 \mathbb E[\zeta_1\zeta_1^\top]=h^2(1-\beta)\mathrm{Id}_d,
\]
while (equation eq:zetacov of the paper) holds for every $k\ge2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.422810+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_198d19a1f904a50181464fd746a601f41002b6c6a1c1a8b66a112277c7c0b3e8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop: asymptotic op val cumulants of arXiv:2607.22156, 'A random matrix approach to lamplighter groups'] Let $r\geq1$, let $b_1,\ldots,b_n\in\mathcal C$ be cactus-type monomials, and let $\epsilon:[n]\to\{1,-1\}$. Then
