{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.965252+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ef5f6895a4713b66d9e83147e2b9a8198f1cbe1067fc72b4ff0ac31c0d3f2f2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem lem:full_supp_meas_full_supp_cop of arXiv:2411.07113, '\begin{LARGE}On differentiability and mass distributions of topologically typical multivar'] Let $C \in \mathcal{C}_{ar}^d$ and let $\gamma \in \mathcal{P}_{\mathcal{W}_d}$ be its corresponding Williamson measure. Then the following assertions hold
