{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:51:15.030908+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2036083ec116341190b038b34799ce52ea4287cd9bb706514fe4e25c255fd8f0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem ChernConnection of arXiv:2609.03909, 'Conic Pseudo-Finslerian Mechanical Systems'] There exists a unique Chern connection and it is characterized by  \textbf{Koszul-type formula}
 \begin{eqnarray*}		2g_V(\nabla^V_XY,Z)&=&Xg_V(Y,Z)-Zg_V(X,Y)+Yg_V(Z,X)\\
