{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.537921+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21d3ad9e9e030e0ce4eadbd19089634332802fc9c110e3fbe7e6ef152e0dd2cd","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 26 (Potter's bound, \protect{\autocite[Theorem 1.5.6) of arXiv:2608.30668, 'Recurrence and capacity of stable branching random walks'] {BinghamGoldieTeugels1987RegularVariation}}]

Let \(f\) be a \(\beta\)-varying function. For all \(C>1\) and
