{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.314524+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_242d80610c85dcac8de99a2acf833b6117670e40b47a5cffa5c4563987341657","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 49 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] Suppose $u: \T^d \to \R^d$ is continuous, $\nabla \cdot u =0$, and for almost every $y \in \T^d$, the ODE
    \[\begin{cases}
    \dot \Phi_t(y) = u(\Phi_t(y)),\\
    \Phi_0(y) = y,
    \end{cases}\]
    admits a unique solution on $(-\infty,\infty)$. Then for any $f \in L^1(\T^d)$ with $f \geq 0$, the continuity equation
    \begin{equation}

    \begin{cases}
        \partial_t \phi + \nabla \cdot (u \phi) = 0,\\
        \phi(0,\cdot) = f(\cdot),
    \end{cases}\end{equation}
    admits a unique distributional solution on $(-\infty,\infty) \times \T^d$ such that $\phi \geq 0$ and for all $T>0,$ $\phi \in \mathcal{C}^0([-T,T],L^1(\T^d))$. Further
    \[\phi(t,\cdot) = (\Phi_t)_* f = f \circ \Phi_{-t},\]
    where $(\Phi_t)_* f$ denotes the pushforward of $f$ as a measure density with respect to Lebesgue, and hence $\phi$ is a renormalized solution in the DiPerna--Lions sense: that is, for all $\beta : \R \to \R$ such that $\beta \in C^1_b(\R)$, $\beta(\phi)$ is also a distributional solution to~\eqref{eq:continuity abstract} with initial data $\beta(f)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.616123+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2436c5a8bbed19fa64f7f3d06e6f322122c7a8d70dc1d98d16c6d871017c6a8e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 (Swapping the local time for GFF) of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Given two naturals $n>k\ge1$, a real $t>0$ and a function $f\in\Cloc^+$, define
\begin{equation}

U_{n,k}(f):=E^\varrho\biggl(\,\prod_{x\in\BbbL_n}\texte^{-f(\theta_n(x),\sqrt{L_t(x)}-m_n,\,\sqrt{L_t(x)}-\sqrt{L_t(x\cdot)}\,)\,1_{\MM_{n,k}(\sqrt{L_t},\,x)}}\biggr)
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}

V_{n,k}(f):=E^\varrho\otimes \wt E\biggl(\,\prod_{x\in\BbbL_n}\texte^{-f(\theta_{n-k}(z),\sqrt{L_t(z)}+h(x)-h(z)-m_n,\,h(x)-h(x\cdot)\,)\,1_{\MM_{n,k}(h,x)\cap \BB_{n,k}(x)}}\biggr),
\end{equation}
where we put $z:=\frakm^k(x)$ to reduce clutter and with the same convention set
 \begin{equation}

\BB_{n,k}(x):=\Bigl\{m_k+k^{1/3}\le m_n-\sqrt{L_t(z)}\le m_k+k^{2/3}\Bigr\}.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}

\lim_{k\to\infty}\limsup_{n\to\infty}\bigl|U_{n,k}(f)-V_{n,k}(f)\bigr|=0
\end{equation}
holds for all $t>0$ and all $f\in\Cloc^{+}$. Moreover, 
\begin{equation}

\lim_{\ell\to\infty}
\limsup_{k \to \infty} \limsup_{n \to \infty} 
P^\varrho\otimes\wt P\biggl(\,\sum_{x\in\BbbL_n}1_{\MM_{n,k}(h,x)\cap \BB_{n,k}(x)}1_{\{\sqrt{L_t(z)}+h(x)-h(z)>m_n-\lambda\}}>\ell\biggr)=0
\end{equation}
holds for all $t>0$ and all~$\lambda>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.750490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24964be5cf1231abdfeedabbce26ae6ddd3082f806d35f283e7861ab80dfbdd4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:anis_length of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] For any $\nu>0$, the norm defined by (equation eq:anis_holder_gen of the paper) is equivalent to the H\"older-Zygmund norm induced by $|\cdot|_B$. In particular, for any $n\in{\mathbb {N}}_0$ and $\alpha\in(0,1)$, we have
\begin{align}
\| f \|_{B,n+\alpha} & \asymp \sum_{\substack{\eta\in {\mathbb {N}}^d_0\\  |\eta  |_{B} \leq n}} \| \partial^\eta f \|_{\infty} +\sum_{\substack{\eta\in {\mathbb {N}}_0^d\\  |\eta|_B = n  }}  \sup_{x,y\in \mathbb{R}^d} \frac{|\partial^{\eta} f(x) - \partial^{\eta} f(y)|}{|x - y|^{\alpha}_B} 
\\
&\quad +\sum_{i=1}^{\mathfrak{r} }\sum_{\substack{\eta\in {\mathbb {N}}_0^d\\ k\in\{0,1\} \\  |\eta|_B = n - (2 i - k) }}  \sup_{x,y\in \mathbb{R}^d} \frac{|\partial^{\eta} f(x) - \partial^{\eta} f(x^0 ,\, \dots \,, x^{i-1}, y^{i}, \, \dots \, ,  y^{\mathfrak{r}})|}{|x - (x^0 ,\, \dots \,, x^{h-1}, y^{h}, \, \dots \, ,  y^{\mathfrak{r}})|^{\alpha + 2i - k}_B},
\end{align}
where $|\eta|_B$ is the \emph{anisotropic length} of $\eta = (\eta^0, \dots, \eta^{\mathfrak{r}}) \in {\mathbb {N}}^d_0$, defined as
\begin{equation}
|\eta|_B := \sum_{i=0}^{\mathfrak{r}} (2i + 1) |\eta^{i}|.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.358301+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24996ec48580db55af9a0734fc45c90ffc25f1db2822e215bfa4bd5cc97cc966","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:isometric-conjugacy of arXiv:2609.00794, 'On operators whose adjoints or second adjoints attain their norms'] Let $X$ and $Y$ be Banach spaces, and let
\[
U\colon \ell_1\to X^*,
\qquad
V\colon \ell_1\to Y^*
\]
be surjective linear isometries. Given $T\in\mathcal L(X,Y)$, put $S:=U^{-1}T^*V\in\mathcal L(\ell_1,\ell_1)$.
    \begin{equation*}
    \begin{tikzcd}
	{Y^* } && {X^*} \\
	{\ell_1} && {\ell_1}
	\arrow["{T^*}", from=1-1, to=1-3]
	\arrow["{U^{-1}}", from=1-3, to=2-3]
	\arrow["V", from=2-1, to=1-1]
	\arrow["S"', from=2-1, to=2-3]
\end{tikzcd}    
    \end{equation*}
Then $\|S\|=\|T\|$, and $T \in \operatorname{NA}_2 (X,Y)$ if and only if $S^* \in \operatorname{NA} (\ell_\infty,\ell_\infty)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.559367+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24c835ad2b95ad68f3286cfed48d467f1cb3c955a03709517afc62423c722a1c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro pro2.1 of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Let the assumptions of (pro2.01 of the paper) hold. Then there exists a constant $C_{\bar{p},\theta}>0$ depending only on $\bar{p}$ and $\theta$ such that for each $0\leq r\leq t< +\infty$,
\begin{align*}
\begin{split}
&\mathbb{E}\left[\sup_{s\in[t\wedge\tau,\tau]}\left(e^{\bar{p}\int_{0}^{s}
\bar{\rho}_{r}{\rm d}r}|y_s|^{\bar{p}}\right)\bigg|\mathcal{F}_{r\wedge\tau}\right]+ \mathbb{E}\left[\left(\int_{t\wedge\tau}^{\tau}e^{2 \int_{0}^{s}\bar{\rho}_r{\rm d}r}|z_s|^2{\rm d}s\right)^\frac{\bar{p}}{2}\bigg|\mathcal{F}_{r\wedge\tau}\right]\\
&\hspace{0.6cm}+\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{t\wedge\tau}^{\tau}\bar{p}e^{\bar{p} \int_{0}^{s}\bar{\rho}_r{\rm d}r}(\bar{\rho}_s-\bar{\mu}_s-\frac{\theta}{2[1\wedge(\bar{p}-1)]}
{\bar\nu_s}^2)|y_s|^{\bar{p}}{\rm d}s\bigg|\mathcal{F}_{r\wedge\tau}\right]\\
&\ \ \leq
C_{\bar{p},\theta}\mathbb{E}\left[e^{\bar{p}\int_{0}^{\tau}\bar{\rho}_{r}{\rm d}r}|\xi|^{\bar{p}}+\left(
\int_{t\wedge\tau}^{\tau}e^{ \int_{0}^{s}\bar{\rho}_r{\rm d}r}f_s{\rm d}s\right)^{\bar{p}}\bigg|\mathcal{F}_{r\wedge\tau}\right].
\end{split}
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.650888+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_251d52df5077e8eb104e11d4f0fa6f711281a4a7561eb930c44053310107b6f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm domain-mon of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $D, \tilde D\subseteq\mathbb C$ be two simply connected domains such that $D\subseteq\tilde D$. Let $\phi$ and $\tilde\phi$ be two GFFs in the respective domains. We have that:
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
        \item For any $\alpha\in(0,\sqrt{2})$ and any $z,w\in D$, 
        \begin{equation}
             \langle :\! \cos(\alpha\phi(z)) \!: :\! \cos(\alpha\phi(w)) \!: \rangle \geq \langle :\! \cos(\alpha\tilde\phi(z)) \!: :\! \cos(\alpha\tilde\phi(w)) \!: \rangle. 
        \end{equation}
        \item For any $\alpha\in(0,1]$ and any $z,w\in D$, 
        \begin{equation}
             \langle :\! \sin(\alpha\phi(z)) \!: :\! \sin(\alpha\phi(w)) \!: \rangle \leq \langle :\! \sin(\alpha\tilde\phi(z)) \!: :\! \sin(\alpha\tilde\phi(w)) \!: \rangle.
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.415473+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_259945f70f47cbb1e71848028060b888d6d58aebf0166a67a19f54b167bcc62c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma limit os Delta z at S_1 of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] Let $(\lambda_n,C^2_n) \to (\lambda,0) \in \partial S_1^\rho$ with $\lambda<p-1$, then
