{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.362976+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_26b46b1daba7225ea16312703235c28d20f3619948a2fb18b324b84088ab809b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 (Expected number of fixed points) of arXiv:2606.18047, 'Analysis of the asymmetric shelf shuffle'] The expected number of fixed points in $\pi\sim\nu_{n, m}^{(p)}$ is
\begin{equation*}
\E_{\nu^{(p)}_{n,m}}[N_1(\pi)]
=\sum_{r=1}^{n}m^{1-r}\bigl(p^r-(-q)^r\bigr)
=\frac{p(1-(p/m)^n)}{1-p/m}+\frac{q(1-(-q/m)^n)}{1+q/m}.

\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.099068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_26bf661bd9cff31647792a10adcec5a0abf656c15ceb93ef4da7cdd5c1f16909","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2601.20502, 'Optimal matching under size priority'] Let $(\mathbb{G}, \mathbf o, \mathbb M )$ be a unimodular random matched rooted graph, we define the performance of $(\mathbb{G},\mathbf o,\mathbb{M})$ as:
    \begin{align*}
     \perfE(\mathbb{G},\mathbf o, \mathbb{M}) &:= \bigg(\mathbb{P}((\mathbf{o}_-,\mathbf{o_+})\in \mathbb{M}), \mathbb{E}\left[ w((\mathbf{o}_-,\mathbf{o}_+))\mathbbm{1}_{(\mathbf{o}_-,\mathbf{o}_+) \in \mathbb{M}} \right]\bigg) \text{ in the edge-rooted setting,}  \\
    \perfV(\mathbb{G},\mathbf o,\mathbb{M}) &:=\bigg(\mathbb{P}( \mathbf{o} \text{ is matched by } \mathbb{M}) ,\mathbb{E}\left[ \sum_{v \sim o}w(\mathbf{o},v)\mathbbm{1}_{(\mathbf{o},v) \in \mathbb{M}} \right] \bigg)\text{in the vertex-rooted setting.} 
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.989600+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_26c4265b248877e53409cb8d8080ae16e437bd1df9e2b6dd73a51d6520ccb548","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 (\cite{DovOrsToaldo}) of arXiv:2604.00882, 'On some extensions of generalized counting processes'] {The density $\ell_\nu(x,t)$ of the process $\mathcal{L}^\nu(t)$, $t > 0$, solves the time-fractional boundary-initial problem}
	\begin{equation}
		\begin{cases}
			\left( \mathbb{D}_t^{2\nu} + 2\lambda \mathbb{D}_t^{\nu}\right) \ell_\nu(x,t) = -\frac{\partial}{\partial x} \ell_\nu(x,t), \quad x > 0,\,\, t > 0,\,\, 0 < \nu < \frac{1}{2}, \\
			\ell_\nu(x,0) = \delta(x), \\
			\ell_\nu(0,t) = \frac{t^{-2\nu}}{\Gamma(1-2\nu)} + 2\lambda \frac{t^{-\nu}}{\Gamma(1-\nu)},
		\end{cases}
	\end{equation}

	{and has $x$-Laplace transform, for $0 < \gamma < \lambda^2$,}
	\begin{equation}
		\widetilde{\ell}_\nu(\gamma, t) = \frac{1}{2} \left[ \left( 1 + \frac{\lambda}{\sqrt{\lambda^2 - \gamma}} \right) E_{\nu,1} (r_1 t^\nu) + \left( 1 - \frac{\lambda}{\sqrt{\lambda^2 - \gamma}} \right) E_{\nu,1} (r_2 t^\nu) \right],
	\end{equation}

	{where}
	\begin{equation}
		r_1 = -\lambda + \sqrt{\lambda^2 - \gamma}, \quad r_2 = -\lambda - \sqrt{\lambda^2 - \gamma}.
	\end{equation}

	{The fractional derivatives appearing in \eqref{2.20} are  in the Riemann-Liouville sense.} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.363713+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_26fff1392f48af6c3f7e294e2f73157fab5a9450358eef64ab38d6c5fa270857","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 (Generating function for inversions) of arXiv:2606.18047, 'Analysis of the asymmetric shelf shuffle'] Let $\pi\sim\nu^{(p)}_{n,m}$.  Then
