{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.331477+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_271f3fcb68277aa18cc9cca129af77cc5a3bb8ca2bf5682f2043d37160d0979a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:wp:pinsker of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Let $\mathcal{X}$ be a Polish space, and $\nu$ and $\nu'$ be probability measures in $\mathcal{P}(\mathcal{X})$. For any non-negative, measurable function $f: \mathcal{X} \rightarrow \ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d$, we have 
