{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:38:25.225240+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2877a435acfe18de58b33b7153dba33cb3770eb4c27adae6ffc568484b9a6d84","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary Quantitative Stability of $I_\gamma^*$ of arXiv:2609.00324, 'Quantitative Stability for Fractional Yamabe minimizers'] Let $(M^n , [\hat{h}])$ be the conformal infinity of an asymptotically hyperbolic manifold $(X^{n+1},g^+ )$ such that $\Lambda_{\gamma} (M,[\hat{h}]) < \Lambda_{\gamma} (\mathbb{S}^n ,[h_{0}])$. Then, there exist constants $C>0$ and $\theta \geq 0$ such that
