{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:04:39.206563+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_287b2ecfd809edcd09e4c0fb1f1ca6e554c2c90db67dbf86c858c28521c32494","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 (Meta-definition of coarse modified log-Sobolev inequality) of arXiv:2608.13677, 'Asymptotically complete free-energy dissipation: \\ a coarse MLSI holds at any positive te'] \label[definition]{definition:coarse_modified_log_sobolev}
    We say that a \emph{coarse modified log-Sobolev inequality} \emph{(coarse MLSI)} holds if for every \(\epsilon > 0\), there is some \(\delta = \delta(\varepsilon) > 0\) such that for all (allowed) initial distributions \(\mu\) it holds that
    \begin{align}
        \sigma(\mu)
        \geq \delta \, ([F(\mu) - \min_\nu F(\nu)] - \epsilon).
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.329436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28957b2461853b8c0488ad23513cabc2b818dada131aefedc0e7f6854619bbe2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem CAF2 of arXiv:2411.06571, 'Moment-based approach for two erratic KPZ scaling limits'] Under $\mathbf E^{(x_1,...,x_n)}_{\mathrm{Cen}(1)},$ each coordinate difference $X^i-X^j$ is a Markov process on $\Bbb R$ with generator $G_{\mathrm{diff}}:= (1- \varphi*\varphi(x))\partial_x^2$.
    Let $\mathbf E_{\mathrm{diff}}^x$ denote expectation with respect to that Markov process, started from $x\in\Bbb R$. There exists some universal constant $C>0$, such that uniformly over all smooth functions $\phi\ge 0$ with $\int_{\Bbb R} \phi =1,$ and all $s,t ,q\ge 0$, one has 
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{x\in\Bbb R} \mathbf E^x_{\mathrm{diff}}\bigg[\bigg|\int_s^t \phi(Y_s)ds\bigg|^q\bigg]^{1/q} &\leq Cq^{1/2} |t-s|^{1/2}\\
        \sup_{x\in\Bbb R} \mathbf E^x_{\mathrm{diff}}[e^{q \int_0^t \phi(Y_s)ds}] &\leq Ce^{Cq^2 t}.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.289384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2897e0074e4b6ddad0e8f13b7c9835bc9134f467f2394f4ce1be2520a6ccd15f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 18 of arXiv:2604.25725, 'What is The Probability That A Random Graph With A Given Degree Sequence is Connected?'] For all $0<\gamma<1$ and $0<\epsilon<10^{-8}$,  if $m$ is large enough and $n_1 \le m^{1-\gamma}$ while $n_2\leq\eps m$ and $2|E(H_i)|+X_i \le \epsilon m$, then
