{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:14:37.640765+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a29af32481ba2680e3bde23c7b70a6c29162c9473b3cda2ec1e4bfb5e2aea32","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Extratheorem 6 of arXiv:2608.19179, 'A random walk on $p$-groups with a symmetric perfect pairing'] \cite[Theorem 2]{Woodetal}
Let $G$ be a finite abelian $p$-group of rank $r$ with a perfect symmetric pairing $<\cdot,\cdot>$. Then:
\[
\probP\Big(\Ker(SymHaar_{n,n}) \cong (G,<\cdot,\cdot>)\Big)= \]
\[\frac{
\prod_{j=n-r+1}^{n} (1-p^{-j}) \prod_{i=1}^{\lceil (n-r)/2 \rceil}(1-p^{1-2i})
}{
\# G
\# Aut(G,<\cdot,\cdot>)
}
\]
where $Aut(G,<\cdot,\cdot>)$ is the group of automorphisms of $G$ that preserve the pairing $<\cdot,\cdot>$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:37:25.934584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2a3bc0a1ae12ad8dee60a20f23c8885766ab1a3e2c20a8aeb3e5aa6223742877","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 41 (Completed Harish--Chandra reflection) of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] For every zero-framed knot $K$ and every integer $n\ge2$, let
