{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:35:57.004086+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ca5334fe482fcdc7fe0cb112bdd0752143b543577b7c2e0e7990f90315a30fa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:E[multi-edges] of arXiv:2604.05921, 'Simplicity of random hypergraphs'] Let $\forall e \in E: \delta_e \leq \frac{1}{2} n \mathds{E}[d_U]$ and let $R(\cdot)$ be as in (equation def:B of the paper). Then the expected number of multi-hyperedge pairs in a uniformly random undirected hypergraph with degree sequence $\vb*{d}$ is
    \begin{align}

        \mathds{E}[M_n]&= \frac{1}{2} \sum_{e \in E} \sum_{\substack{e' \in E\backslash\{e\}:\\\delta_{e'}=\delta_e}}\frac{(n\mathds{E}[d_U]-2\delta_e)!}{(n \mathds{E}[d_U])!}\sum_{\substack{\vb*{a} \in \mathds{N}^{\delta_e}:\\\sum_{i=1}^{\delta_e} ia_i = \delta_e}}  \frac{\delta_e!^2}{\prod_{k=1}^{\delta_e} k!^{2a_k} }\sum_{\alpha(\cdot) \in R(\vb*{a})} (-1)^{\sum_{\vb*{x} \in \mathds{N}^{\delta_e}} (\sum_{i=1}^{\delta_e} x_i - 1)\alpha(\vb*{x})} \\
     &\hspace{1cm}\times 
    \prod_{\vb*{y} \in \mathds{N}^{\delta_e}} \Bigg( \frac{1}{\alpha(\vb*{y})!} \Big(\frac{n\mathds{E}\big[\prod_{i=1}^{\delta_e} (\mathds{1}_{\{d_U \geq 2i\}}\frac{d_U!}{(d_U-2i)!})^{y_i} \big]\big(\sum_{i=1}^{\delta_e} y_i-1 \big)!}{\prod_{i=1}^{\delta_e} y_i!} \Big)^{\alpha(\vb*{y})} \Bigg). \nonumber
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:04:07.033322+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2cb063a4de6327fb20ca9a57c8d18022e41d7cdf6fb3b605544f3cda60e3e403","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:SIR_monotonicity of arXiv:2607.29409, 'The Zombie Infection Model'] Let $G_{1} = (V_{1}, E_{1})$ and $G_{2} = (V_{2}
