{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.614194+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2cd6842472efc7395e45eec967cf9a1af9bc002d919b9f6f74bee99d91dc8caf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Transition trajectories and transition path process share the same distribution) of arXiv:2506.09462, 'Transition Path Theory For L\'{e}vy-Type Processes: SDE Representation and Statistics'] Let \(X_t\) satisfy the L\'{e}vy SDE \eqref{eqn:SDE}, and let \(Y^n\) denote the \(n\)-th \(A \to B\) transition trajectory defined by \eqref{eqn:reactive}. Let \(Y_t\) be the process defined in Theorem \ref{theo:TPPSDE}. Then, for any bounded and continuous functional \(H: C([0, \infty)) \to \mathbb{R}\), we have  
