{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.589109+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d6985fd8a1da9aba5cf7f280ede465d546d897bec12dcfb7d1dcddd7169e7c8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor temper of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Assume that $D(\mathcal F_{\beta})\neq \emptyset$.
    For $0<\beta<\beta'$ let $\mathsf{P}_{\beta}$ and $\mathsf{P}_{\beta'}$ be the unique minimizers of $\mathcal F_{\beta}$ and $\mathcal F_{\beta'}$ on $\mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ respectively. Set $\Pi_\beta:= \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}_\beta)$ and $\Pi_{\beta'}:= \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}_{\beta'})$ and assume that there exists $p'\geq p$ such that $\int  \mathsf{s}_0^{p'}\Pi_\beta(d \mathsf{s}),\int  \mathsf{s}_0^{p'}\Pi_{\beta'}(d \mathsf{s})<\infty$. Then \begin{align}
       \mathscr W_p^2(\mathsf{P}_{\beta},\mathsf{P}_{\beta'})\leq \frac{2(\beta'-\beta)}{\beta}\max\left(\int f( \mathsf{s}_0)^{\frac{p}{p-2}}\Pi_\beta(d \mathsf{s}) ,\int f( \mathsf{s}_0)^{\frac{p}{p-2}}\Pi_{\beta'}(d \mathsf{s}) \right)^{\frac{2-p}{p}}\mathcal W^{int}(\mathsf{P}_{\beta})
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.729690+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d7b58782ee105b778aac885ac5bd5b3ad339c9ad6f89a47e64268eff9b36307","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem nah-an-opt of arXiv:2503.22334, 'Probabilistic analysis of optimal multi-pivot QuickSort'] The additional cost of the algorithm compared to always using $t_{\mathrm{opt}}$ is of sub-polynomial order:
