{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.556878+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2e907f2597724d802b1d06a47f9bc078740410e1f2421fd76308ad189fdf3792","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2608.27156, 'Traveling Waves in Equity Markets with\\Rank-Based Entry and Exit'] In the setting of Theorem~\ref{thm:wave}, let $\alpha$ be the tail exponent \eqref{eq:alpha-main} of Corollary~\ref{cor:tail}, and let $0 \leq p < \alpha$. Then
\begin{equation}
    G^p \;=\; c \;+\; (1 - p)\, G^p_* \;+\; \Big\langle \frac{\tilde f}{g},\, \bar\Pi^p \Big\rangle \;-\; \big\langle \lambda_d,\, \bar\Pi^p \big\rangle,
    \qquad
