{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.192751+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2eee24047157e614aef8827e7340b024bf743f93c6d0ae843a600fcd2e5694a1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (Multiple moment matching) of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] Let $\chi$ be either real or complex random variable such that $\E |\chi|^p<\infty$ for any $p\in\N$. Assume that $\chi$ has non-degenerate support in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:support}. Then for any fixed $\Gamma\in\N$ and for sufficiently small, possibly $\Gamma$-dependent $\alpha>0$, there exists a random variable $\chi_\alpha$ with compactly supported distribution, such that
\begin{equation}
