{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.296765+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ef393666ab9ab7c87d95ed5421716846ba1796d1ae032658b5d19c915ce562e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Red of arXiv:2605.10452, 'A secretary for Messrs. Luce and Mallows'] {\bf(CDK)}
Let $\{V_j\}_{j=1}^n$ be independent exponential random variables with $V_j\sim\text{Exp}(\theta_j),\ j\in[n]$.
Then
\begin{equation}
P\left(\text{Red}(V_1V_2\cdots V_n)=\sigma\right)=P_n^{\mathcal{L}_\text{inv};\{\theta_j\}_{j=1}^n}(\sigma),
\end{equation}
where $\text{Red}(V_1V_2\cdots V_n)$ is the reduced permutation in $S_n$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.045229+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f00aa8de79bc5c32986170f724b00bf21766f62213a446e2fcc5527dc509ad6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:gaussianTVrate of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] Let
\begin{equation*}
 Y_{n+1}=MY_n+G\xi_{n+1}
\end{equation*}
be a Gaussian autoregressive process on $\mathbb R^N$, with transition kernel $Q$, where $M\in\mathbb R^{N\times N}$ satisfies $\rho(M)<1$, $G\in\mathbb R^{N\times N'}$, the $\xi_n$ are i.i.d.\ standard Gaussian vectors in $\mathbb R^{N'}$, and the covariance $\Sigma_{n_0}$ of the $n_0$-step transition law is nonsingular for some $n_0\ge1$; this holds in particular when $GG^\top\succ0$, with $n_0=1$. Then the chain has a unique invariant law $\pi$, which is a centered Gaussian. Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \limsup_{n\to\infty}\lVert \delta_zQ^n-\pi\rVert_{\mathrm{TV}}^{1/n}\le\rho(M)
 \qquad\text{for every initial state }z,
\end{equation}
and the limit exists and equals $\rho(M)$ for a suitable $z$. Finally, there are initial states $z,\widetilde z$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \lim_{n\to\infty}
 \norm{\delta_zQ^n-\delta_{\widetilde z}Q^n}_{\mathrm{TV}}^{1/n}=\rho(M).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.299559+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f158abbabfd214a9f2f05e86725b2c4c29d7123f10f581f5b097f79424aff2f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:results:stationary of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] We say $\nu \in {\mathcal{M}_{\kappa, d}}$ is a \emph{stationary distribution} of the $\kappa$-MLFE{} with potentials $(U, W)$ if $\nu \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$ and there exists a linear growth solution $(\mu^\nu, \gamma)$ to the $\kappa$-MLFE{} on $[0, \infty)$ with potentials  $(U, W)$ and initial condition $\nu$ such that
    \begin{equation}

        \mu^\nu_t = \nu,\quad t \geq 0.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:09:59.300988+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f1d7fe79b812ded0873e415f91e5042b41810d2556add4c0a8edad6a494c34b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem of arXiv:2608.06500, 'Free energy of Ising models under a spectral condition'] For any $\varepsilon,t,\delta>0$, and an $\alpha$-good potential $V$,
     there exists a local function
    $q_{\varepsilon}:\mathcal{G}_{[0,C],C}\times[0,1]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^N$ which can be written
    as a finite sum

    \begin{align*}
    \text{\boldmath $q$}_{\varepsilon}(G;\beta) = \sum_{X\in\mathcal{S}} c_X(\beta) \text{\boldmath $t$}(X,G)\, ,
    \end{align*}
    such that $\mathcal{S}$ is a finite set, the coefficients $c_X(\beta)$
    are  polynomials in $\beta$ independent of $G$, and 
    for all $G\in\mathcal{G}_{[0,C],C}$ and $\beta\in[0,1]$, we have (for $K=t/\delta$)

    \begin{align*}
    \left| \frac{1}{N}\mathbb{E}[H(\text{\boldmath $\psi$}^{(K)})] - q_{\varepsilon} (G;\beta) \right| \le \varepsilon.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.428431+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f39b694d0d8c59d30d8e665af3ba20ba3aea4d961bc1cba82f8564d7e3e9464","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma estimates for gprime and gbis at 1 of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] We have
