{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.995182+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36837208235239dfbd8c9ca4fc84cfbc4d50098fc04f47e06e247e67e530b1e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm P loc dim of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] Almost surely under $\hat{P}_{\bm{\rho}}$, for every $t \in (0,\infty)$,
