{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.121594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3870bdacb06822a50a09f0c3712f958f248e84d500391a553b48ad1ea924a062","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro of arXiv:2601.20502, 'Optimal matching under size priority'] Let $(\mathbb{T},o)$ be a UBGW with Poisson $\mathcal{P}(c)$ reproduction law with $c<e$.
    Let $(G_n,o_n)$ be a sequence of random weighted graphs converging locally in total variation to $(\mathbb{T},o)$. Define $\mathcal{M}_{\max}(G_n)$ to be the set of maximal matchings on $(G_n)$
    We then have the following convergence:
        \begin{equation}
            \begin{aligned}
                \frac{1}{|E(G_n)|} \sum_{e \in E(G_n)} \mathbbm{1}_{\forall \mathbb{M} \in \mathcal{M}_{\max}(G_n), e \in \mathbb{M}} &\overset{\mathbb{P}}{\longrightarrow} \gamma^2, \\
                 \frac{1}{|E(G_n)|} \sum_{e \in E(G_n)} \mathbbm{1}_{\forall \mathbb{M} \in \mathcal{M}_{\max}(G_n), e \notin \mathbb{M}} &\overset{\mathbb{P}}{\longrightarrow} (1-\gamma)^2.
            \end{aligned}
        \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.582190+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_387f185cd18b131b117cf71267df304b870fc9c801de2b436c68609093173990","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm intro1 of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1$ be the laws of two stationary point processes with unit intensity and $\mathcal F_\beta(\mathsf{P}_i)<\infty$ for $i=0,1.$ Then, there is an interpolation $(\mathsf{P}_t)_{t\in[0,1]}$ between $\mathsf{P}_0$ and $\mathsf{P}_1$ and a coupling $ \mathsf{Q}^0$ between the Palm measures of $\mathsf{P}_0$ and $\mathsf{P}_1$ such that 
\begin{align}  
    \mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{t})\leq  (1-t)\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{0})+t\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{1})-\frac{(1-t)t\beta}{2}\int \sum_{(0,0)\neq (x,y)\in \bar\xi} (x-y)^2\inf_{z\in [x,y]}f(\left\lvertz\right\rvert) \mathsf{Q}^0(d\bar\xi),
    \end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.342117+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3890123a0cd60878a5028a14a268f253f23515248aea4ab0b7be0a06383c6396","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:hypE of arXiv:2412.01381, 'Ergodicity and mixing for locally monotone stochastic evolution equations'] If $A=A_0+F$ where $A_0=-\partial \Phi$ is the subgradient of a lower semi-continuous convex functional $\Phi:V\to \mathbb{R}$ such that $\inf_{u\in V}\Phi(u)>-\infty$, and $F:V\to V^\ast$ is a strongly measurable (nonlinear) operator.
Suppose that
for some constants $\kappa_1\in\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}$, $K_1\in\mathbb{R}$
that for every $u\in V$,
\begin{equation}\|F (u)\|_{V^\ast}\le \kappa_1\langle A_0 u,u\rangle+K_1.\end{equation}
Furthermore, suppose that for some constants $K_2,\kappa_2\in\mathbb{R}$, for every $u\in V$, 
\begin{equation}2\langle F(u),u\rangle\le\kappa_2\|F (u)\|_{V^\ast}+K_2,\end{equation}
