{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:48:24.296122+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3c041e77b3253edc758686c299bce7f6b859fd0a44dda8b61690da7fd8e82d80","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition BrussresultMallows of arXiv:2605.10452, 'A secretary for Messrs. Luce and Mallows'] For each $n\in\mathbb{N}$, consider the secretary problem for the Mallows distribution $P_n^{\mathcal{M};q}$, $q\in(0,\infty)$, when either the largest number or the smallest number is of highest rank. For each of these problems, denote by $M_n^*$ an optimal strategy.
