{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.289294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e9c96945fbd490fd72571fcbc8d8d012072fdc460ba6ce58865fef1a34915a8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 17 of arXiv:2604.25725, 'What is The Probability That A Random Graph With A Given Degree Sequence is Connected?'] Let $0<\eps<10^{-6}$ and assume $\cD$ is such that $m$ is large enough and that $n_1,n_2<\epsilon m$. Suppose that for some  $i\geq1$, $|E(H_{i-1})| \le \frac{m}{10^{5}}$ and   $X_{i-1}<10^{-4}m$.  
    Then for any nonnegative $j,k$ with $j+k \le \frac{\sqrt{m}}{1000}$, the probability, conditioning on $H_{i-1}$, of the event $\Bad_{j,k}^{(i)}$ is at most
\begin{equation}
\frac{jm}{jm-2ed_i(v_i)n_1}\left(\frac{2ed_i(v_i)n_1}{jm}\right)^{j}\frac{km}{km-10ed_i(v_i)n_2}\left(\frac{10ed_i(v_i)n_2}{km}\right)^{k}
\end{equation}
if $j,k>0$, $2ed_i(v_i)n_1<jm$, and $10ed_i(v_i)n_2<km$; at most
\begin{equation}
  \frac{km}{km-10ed_i(v_i)n_2}\left(\frac{10ed_i(v_i)n_2}{km}\right)^{k}
\end{equation}
if $j=0$ and $10ed_i(v_i)n_2<km$; and at most
\begin{equation}
  \frac{jm}{jm-2ed_i(v_i)n_1}\left(\frac{2ed_i(v_i)n_1}{jm}\right)^{j}
\end{equation}
if $k=0$ and $2ed_i(v_i)n_1<jm$.
Furthermore, for any $\ell\geq1$, the probability, conditioning on $H_{i-1}$, of the event $\Bad_{j,k}^{(i)}\cap\{L_i\geq\ell\}$ is at most 
\begin{equation}
p^{(i)}_{j,k}\left(\frac{2d_i(v_i)X_{i-1}}{\ell m}\right),
\end{equation}
where $p^{(i)}_{j,k}$ (depends on $j$, $k$, and $H_{i-1}$ via $d_i(v_i)$) is equal to the minimum of $1$ and \eqref{eq:jk}, \eqref{eq:k}, or \eqref{eq:j} if their respective assumptions are satisfied.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.500887+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3eac353244798fc100936950f1105a77fa7285ef0f6d30e80931b7dfd53289be","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition D:geo of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Let $X:\mathbb{Z}^2 \to \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}\cup\{\infty\}$ be a field of random variables that are independent subject to the symmetry condition $X(i,j)=X(j,i)$ for all $i,j$, and distributed as follows.

\textbf{Exponential setting.}
Take real parameters $\alpha$ and $\{\gamma_i\}_{i\in\mathbb{Z}}$. For any $i\in\mathbb{Z}$, take $X(i,i)\sim \operatorname{Exp}(\alpha+\gamma_i)$ if $\alpha+\gamma_i>0$, and $X(i,i)=\infty$ otherwise.  
For any $i\neq j\in\mathbb{Z}$, take $X(i,j)=X(j,i)\sim \operatorname{Exp}(\gamma_i+\gamma_j)$ if $\gamma_i+\gamma_j>0$, and $X(i,j)=X(j,i)=\infty$ otherwise.

\textbf{Geometric setting.}
Take positive parameters $\alpha$ and $\{\gamma_i\}_{i\in\mathbb{Z}}$. For any $i\in\mathbb{Z}$, take $X(i,i)\sim \operatorname{Geo}(\alpha\gamma_i)$ if $\alpha\gamma_i\in(0,1)$, and $X(i,i)=\infty$ otherwise.  
For any $i\neq j\in\mathbb{Z}$, take $X(i,j)=X(j,i)\sim \operatorname{Geo}(\gamma_i\gamma_j)$ if $\gamma_i\gamma_j\in(0,1)$, and $X(i,j)=X(j,i)=\infty$ otherwise.

For any $u\le v$ in $\mathbb{Z}^2$, define the \emph{passage time}
\[
X(u;v)=\max_{\pi}\sum_{(i,j)\in\pi}X(i,j),
\]
where the maximum is taken over all up-right paths $\pi$ from $u$ to $v$ satisfying (equation E:diagonal-condition of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:51:11.955674+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ec854e08729401fade6c9bc67b028c4fc4958bda51c6b5856c42fd1778abd0c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 36 (Fourier--Duhamel trace derivative bound) of arXiv:2608.07820, 'Linear Spectral Statistics for Entrywise-Transformed Spiked Wigner Matrices under Shifted '] Let \(h\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb R)\), let \(A=A^{\mathsf T}\), and let
\(B=B^{\mathsf T}\).  For every integer \(r\ge1\),
\begin{equation}
 \sup_{u\in\mathbb R}
 \left|\frac{\dd^r}{\dd u^r}\Tr h(A+uB)\right|
 \le
 C_{h,r}\norm{B}_1\norm{B}_{\op}^{r-1},
\end{equation}
where
