The constant is independent of the dimension and of \(A\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.023222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ec9b79c071e8898fe7e34aaedfe2ffca97e03f80a90b6bcce6e2dda9f7805b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro 4 (\protect{\cite[Theorem 1.2) of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] {Azagra2023}}]
	Let $\Omega \subset \R^n$ be an open and convex set, and let $\phi \in \operatorname{SCL}(\Omega)$.
	Then for any $x \in \operatorname{Diff}(\phi)$ and any symmetric real $n \times n$ matrix $A$,
	we have
	\begin{align*}
		\lim_{y \to x} \frac{\bigl|\phi(y) - \phi(x) - \langle D\phi(x), y-x \rangle
			- \tfrac{1}{2} \langle A(y-x), y-x \rangle\bigr|}{|y-x|^2} = 0
	\end{align*}
	if and only if
	\begin{align*}
		\lim_{y \to x} \sup_{p \in D^{+}\phi(y)} \frac{|p - D\phi(x) - A(y-x)|}{|y-x|} = 0.
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.298687+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f033a68a807affd1458f3ea82e44685e9daad964891366ab823487b2dc42459","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 (Existence) of arXiv:2606.23383, 'Near-Lipschitz stability of the Kim--Milman flow map'] Let $\nu \in \cP_2(\R^d)$, and let $\{\nu_n\}_{n\in\N}$ be a regular approximating sequence for $\nu$ (see Definition~\ref{def:reg_approx}).
    Then, for every $t > 0$, the $L^2(\gamma)$ limit $\KM^\nu_{t\gets} \deq \lim_{n\to\infty} \KM^{\nu_n}_{t\gets}$ exists, is independent of the approximating sequence $\{\nu_n\}_{n\in\N}$, and $(\KM^\nu_{t\gets})_\sharp \gamma = q_t^\nu$.

    Moreover, $\KM^\nu \deq \lim_{t\searrow 0} \KM^\nu_{t\gets}$ exists in $L^2(\gamma)$, and $(\KM^\nu)_\sharp \gamma = \nu$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.243062+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f3505893076c029c829dda74399dd4a04a688dcef77fd6da7a3f1eadf07fda2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem inf of arXiv:2604.23751, 'Large deviation principles for pattern-avoiding permutations, and limit shapes for constra'] Let us consider two sets $A$ and $B$ and a function $h$ on $A \cup B$.
It holds that
\begin{equation}
\inf_{z \in A \cup B} h(z) +\inf_{z \in A \cap B} h(z)
\ge \inf_{z \in A} h(z) + \inf_{z \in B} h(z).
\end{equation}
Moreover, if the inequality is strict, then
\begin{equation}
    \inf_{z \in A} h(z) = \inf_{z \in A \backslash B} h(z) < \inf_{z \in A \cap B} h(z),
\end{equation}
and the same holds if we switch the roles of $A$ and $B$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.278497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f4d7c82d689f261244387e6ae0dafe61fdc27d6ac0a26dc9996817862dcfd8a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq: decomposition of W of arXiv:2411.05924, 'Non-negative Martingale Solutions to the Stochastic Porous Medium Equation with Sticky Beh'] $\widetilde W$ and $\widetilde W_n$ are $Q$--Wiener processes adapted to the filtrations $\widetilde{\mathbb F}$ and $\widetilde{\mathbb F}_n$, respectively, which can be rewritten as
