{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.388964+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3f505c70d8c589eed778f374479e16c76fcf63b9d63c978d50df1914508764a4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:error of arXiv:2412.06452, 'Time-dependent queue length distribution in queues fed by $K$ customers in a finite interv'] For a given $\epsilon$ $(\epsilon \in (0,1])$, 
