{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.614468+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4053fe06a1294dee21c980d6e631d826b37b50e1e3a057b35bc68c6a6946dfbb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 (Probability density of transition trajectories) of arXiv:2506.09462, 'Transition Path Theory For L\'{e}vy-Type Processes: SDE Representation and Statistics'] The \textbf{distribution of transition trajectories} from \(A\) to \(B\), denoted by \(\rho_{\mathcal{R}_{A \to B}} = (\rho_{\mathcal{R}_{A \to B}}(x))_{x \in \Theta}\), is defined such that for any \(x \in \Theta\),  
