{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.617715+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_40a6eec61745de90a2896765778a8d46a9f448f7e7f5e039497e8626ae4051b6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 30 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Let~$X$ be as in Proposition~\ref{prop-6.1}. For each~$\epsilon>0$ and $\sigma\in(0,1/\10)$ there exists~$a_1\ge1$ such that for all~$a\ge a_1$ and all non-negative~$\gamma$ satisfying \eqref{E:4.31},
