\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:29.000362+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_426bd2fcd11b9f368805a6c28769ec1f16a1530714f87fd6924cd80fe75b1bd1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem CM mom UB of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] For any $r \in (0, e^{-1} \wedge r_*)$, $n \in \mathbb{N}$, and $t \in (0, \infty)$,
