{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.648018+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42a3e3c2eb274417b4bfee2305bffa36de7313541257a1e78ed84a3cdf3c16c4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem trick1RWRW of arXiv:2411.13926, 'Random walks on random walks:\\ non-perturbative results in high dimensions'] Consider the RWRW on $\mathbb{Z}^d$, $d\geq 5$, with density $\lambda>0$. Then there is $C <\infty$ such that, and for any $n\in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$,
