{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:25:40.342952+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42d918f39b4173aa8235f07455f2dbc6de1f0c0fcfafd6ff90a0978598bff6d1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: connected cutsets of arXiv:2503.21737, 'High-intensity Voronoi percolation on manifolds'] Let $M$ be simply connected. Let $G=(V,E)$ be a graph such that $V\subset M$. Assume that to each $x\in V$ we can associate an open connected set $O(x)\subset M$ containing $x$ such that
\begin{enumerate}[i)]
\item $\bigcup_{x\in V}O(x)=M$,
\item $O(x)\cap O(y)\ne \emptyset $ if and only if $\{x,y\}\in E$ (for $x\neq y$).
\end{enumerate}
    Then for all $x,y\in V$, any minimal cutset separating $x$ from $y$ is connected in $G$.

    If we further assume that $G$ is one-ended and locally finite\footnote{We call a graph $G=(V,E)$ \emph{one-ended} if for any finite set $\Gamma\subset V$ the induced subgraph on $V\setminus \Gamma$ has a unique infinite connected component.
    We call \(G\) \emph{locally finite} when each of its vertices has finite degree.}
    (which holds, for instance, if $M$ itself is one-ended, the sets $O(x)$ are all bounded and any bounded set \(B \subset M\) intersects at most finitely many of the sets \(O(x)\)), then any minimal cutset separating $x$ from infinity is connected in $G$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.852282+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42eaa6e92444e6194379d7aeb2d9091ed5c35b5f7b477feabf3c3641489844dc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 10 (Secular equation for the eigenvalues) of arXiv:2511.12623, 'The eigenvector bead process'] If $g_j=0$ for some $j$, then $\lambda^{(N)}_j$ remains an eigenvalue of $H_{N+1}$ with eigenvector
$(u^{(N)}_j,0)$. All other eigenvalues of $H_{N+1}$ are the simple zeros of the secular function
\begin{equation}
f(z):=g_{N+1}-z-\sum_{j=1}^N \frac{|g_j^{(N)}|^2}{\lambda^{(N)}_j-z}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.327546+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43084f6a1d86d86ce3612570222dfd4977f8a16e500490732c0f7cd88e39d682","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition e.Stratification of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] We say that ${\mathbb G}$ is a \emph{Carnot group} of step $k$ if ${\mathbb G}$  is a connected and simply connected Lie group whose Lie algebra $\mathfrak{g}$ is \emph{stratified}, that is, there are non-trivial linear subspaces $V_1,\ldots, V_k$ of $\mathfrak{g}$ such that
\begin{align*}
\mathfrak{g}=V_{1}\oplus\cdots\oplus V_{k},
\end{align*}
and
\begin{align}
& \left[V_{1}, V_{i-1}\right]=V_{i},\hskip0.1in  V_{i} \neq \{0\}, \hskip0.1in 2 \leqslant i \leqslant k,
\notag
\\
& [ V_{1}, V_{k} ]=\left\{ 0 \right\}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.301380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4313134e151945e67dd1e8d9eb727bf4e622d08446be427d707228c2ba1e1e9f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:resultunknownmask of arXiv:2602.11129, 'Information-Theoretic Thresholds for Bipartite Latent-Space Graphs Under Noisy Observation'] Consider any fixed $p \in (0,1)$. Then, the following holds whenever $d \gg \log(n)^3$.

    \vspace{0.5em}
    If $p \neq \frac{1}{2}$ then:\hspace{1em} $\begin{aligned}[t]
            \dtv{\mathbb{W}(n, m, q, p, d)}{ \mathbb{M}(n, m, p)} &= \begin{cases} 1 - o(1) & \text{if } d \ll nmq^4  \hspace{1.3cm} \text{ or } \hspace{.1cm} d \ll m\sqrt{n}q^2   \\
            o(1) & \text{if } d \gg nmq^4\log(n) \hspace{.1cm} \text{ and } \hspace{.1cm} d \gg m\sqrt{n}q^2 \log(n)
            \end{cases}
