\end{equation}
Thus the HCM range is exactly the central gamma line.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:27:56.785619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43d9f374574f47b95bcbae9c495fe1002cb6afd5c0cec25674ddb312de18f8c8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 39 (Traces on timelike hypersurfaces) of arXiv:2608.31171, '\bf Finite-energy spacetimes with torus symmetry. \\ \Large Cauchy stability of Einstein--'] Let $I=(t_0,t_1)$ and let $A,B\in L^1(I\times\Sbb^1)$ satisfy
\bel{eq:rect-bal}
\del_tA+\del_xB=\mu
\ee
in distributions, where $\mu$ is a finite Radon measure. For every $\varphi\in C_c^1(I)$, the function
\bel{eq:rect-Bphi}
x\longmapsto B_\varphi(x)
\coloneqq
\int_I B(t,x)\varphi(t)\,dt
\ee
has a $\BV(\Sbb^1)$ representative. Its precise representative defines a distributional normal trace $\operatorname{Tr}_xB$ on every timelike line $x=\mathrm{const}$. If $B\geq0$, these traces are non-negative Radon measures in~$t$. If, in addition, $A$ has the one-sided traces on spacelike hypersurfaces supplied by \autoref{prop-weak-integrated-current}, then
\bel{eq:rect-trace-bound}
\sup_{x\in\Sbb^1}\|\operatorname{Tr}_xB\|_{\Meas(I)}
\leq C\left(
\|B\|_{L^1(I\times\Sbb^1)}
+\|A(t_0+)\|_{L^1(\Sbb^1)}
+\|A(t_1-)\|_{L^1(\Sbb^1)}
+|\mu|(I\times\Sbb^1)
\right),
\ee
where $C$ depends only on the period of the spatial circle. The same conclusion holds for a weighted balance law after its positive weights have been included in $A$ and~$B$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.479027+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43f1174738312d92b973a05c9418c3b1b8cb78a72ac72a9e85a7c9f3509a0d5d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:closed of arXiv:2606.21591, '\textbf{Equal probabilities maximize the expected deficit\\ in the siblings of the coupon '] For every $\mathbf{p}\in\mathcal{P}_N$ and integer $j\ge 2$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}[U_j^N]
=\sum_{\varnothing\ne A\subseteq\{1,\dots,N\}}(-1)^{|A|-1}\,
\frac{\sum_{i\in A}p_i^{\,j}}{\bigl(\sum_{i\in A}p_i\bigr)^{j}} .
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.320454+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43f66941c0edb768f6907fc363b3e10d25a68f7b0aa2e5c9dacf9ab5c35e3ee8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:results:Tn2 of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] For $n \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, define the \emph{truncated 2-tree} $\mathbb{T}_2^n := (V_n, E_n)$  with
