{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.117019+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4597fc6eb5695a4eba731556bb9898bbca57bea123d5bf02b1078d3d2911f637","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2608.27433, 'Scalar curvature on K\"ahler blow-ups and systolic inequalities'] The following estimates hold uniformly for small $\eps$.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item If $k>2$ and $4-2k<\delta<0$, then
