{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.292407+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_48054dfe4928ef50dbefefde6fb6f2e755760178a3a4a25f6b7d3db1795666b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:M2_bound of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Consider $|z_j|\le\sqrt{x_j}-\theta$ and $w_j\in \mathbf{C}\setminus\mathbf{R}$ for $j=1,2$. For any $B_1,B_2\in\mathbf{C}^{(2k_1)\times (2k_1)}$ it holds that
\begin{equation}
x_1\left\vert\left\langle M_{1\widetilde{2}}^{B_1}B_2\right\rangle\right\vert \le \|B_1\|\|B_2\|\sqrt{\frac{x_1\pi\rho_1}{\eta_1}\frac{x_2\pi\rho_2}{\eta_2}}.

\end{equation}
Assume further that $|\Re w_j|\le c\eta_j$ for sufficiently small $c>0$. Then we have
\begin{equation}
x_1\left\vert \left\langle M_{1\widetilde{2}}^{E_\sigma}B\right\rangle\right\vert + x_1\left\vert \left\langle M_{1\widetilde{2}}^{B}E_\sigma\right\rangle\right\vert \lesssim \left(|x_1-x_2|+|z_1-z_2|+|w_1|+|w_2|\right)\|B\|\sqrt{\frac{x_1\pi\rho_1}{\eta_1}\frac{x_2\pi\rho_2}{\eta_2}},

\end{equation}
for $\sigma:=\mathrm{sgn}(\Im w_1\Im w_2)$ and $E_\sigma:=E_\sigma^{(k_1)}$. This bound holds uniformly in $x_j\in [c_0,1]$ with $x_1\le x_2$, $|z_j|< \sqrt{x_j}$, for any fixed $c_0>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.760770+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_481e658cfbb1e8bbd93e09e4711788a01f15f7042072afa9fac9505fa34eaca8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2609.00448, 'Equivariant formality and representation theory'] \textnormal{(cf. \cite[Theorem 6.2]{CFok}).}
