{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.562158+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_494460478f8ad8c4333332ab231907f7f06c7bd12d300a0e469ddfddccfdc3b8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 3.2 of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Let $\xi, \xi'\in L_\tau^p(\rho_\cdot;{\mathbb R}^k)$, both $g$ and $g'$ be the generator of BSDEs satisfying assumptions (A:H4 of the paper) and (A:H5 of the paper), and $(Y_\cdot,Z_\cdot)$ and $(Y_\cdot',Z_\cdot')$ be the weighted $L^p$ solution of BSDE$(\xi,\tau,g)$ and BSDE$(\xi',\tau,g')$, respectively, in the space of $H_\tau^p(\rho_\cdot;{\mathbb R}^{k}\times{\mathbb R}^{k\times d})$.
Then there exists a constant $C_{p,\theta}>0$ depending only on $p$ and $\theta$ such that
\begin{align*}
