{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.989436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a0022dc509ddea88ef4e5017a5657d40a247f2b3ec4ec5894d189201725fe0d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 (\cite{DiC}) of arXiv:2604.00882, 'On some extensions of generalized counting processes'] The solution $\tilde p_j^\nu(t)$ of the Cauchy problem \eqref{Dic1}--\eqref{Dic2}, for $j \in \mathbb{N}_0, \nu \in (0,1]$ and $t \ge 0$, is given by
