Moreover, for any finite $K$, \eqref{eq:limit_rank_one_beta} holds jointly for $k = 1, 2, \dotsc, K$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.291932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a4827f8ea236c111b1f23f82e328e0231984c5b15f167f4d67b7a1bb97b27bb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem annLDPthm of arXiv:2603.22652, 'A cohesive account on the ergodic behaviours and scaling limits of Random Walks in Cooling'] Let $\tau$ be a resampling map, let $X = (X_n, n \in {\mathbb {N}})$ follow the law of the annealed RWCRE defined in (equation eq:annealed_rwcre of the paper), and let $\mu_n$ be the probability measure on ${\mathbb {R}}$ defined by $\mu_n(A): = {\mathbb {P}}(X_n/n \in A)$. 

If there is a function $\Lambda: {\mathbb {R}}\to {\mathbb {R}}$ that is strictly convex and such that
for all $\theta \in {\mathbb {R}}$,
\begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
        \lim_n \frac{1}{n} \log {\mathbb {E}}[e^{\theta X_n}]&= \lim_n \sum_k \frac{T_{k,n}}{n} \frac{1}{T_{k,n}} \log {\mathbb {E}}[e^{\theta Z_{T_{k,n}}}] = \Lambda(\theta).
