{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:23.371092+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a508cc184db09dc4a69fa2226ac838e9f7f6106f617f09a360178fb8e3438cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2512.08595, 'Small time asymptotics of spectral heat content of isotropic processes'] Let $X=(X_t)_{t\ge 0}$ be a translation invariant, isotropic stochastic process on $\R^d$ satisfying Assumption~\ref{assump1}. Then for any nonnegative $f\in C^{1,\kappa}_c(\R^d)$,
