{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.116476+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ad4786d455e2903da74ce382e579f2cbf30d320ec4af5218073348fc4171420","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 of arXiv:2608.27433, 'Scalar curvature on K\"ahler blow-ups and systolic inequalities'] Let \(d(x)=\dist_\omega(x,S)\). At every $p\in S$, there are holomorphic coordinates $(z_1,\ldots,z_k,w_1,\ldots,w_{n-k})$, centered at $p$, such that $S=\{z=0\}$,
