{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.094502+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_54410154748c7ec685d5a22d524e567dec373b697111caf18d79caf572727daa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem L:under:P:mu:w of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Let $(\mu,\overline{{\mathrm{w}}}):=(\mu,{\mathrm{w}},\resizebox{3 mm}{2.5mm}{$\curlywedge$})\in \overline{\Theta}_x$. Under $\mathbb{P}^\dag_{\mu , \overline{{\mathrm{w}}}}$, the convergence (equation equation:aproximacionL*Pmu of the paper) holds. Moreover, if under $\mathbb{P}^\dag_{\mu , \overline{{\mathrm{w}}}}$ we consider $(a_i,b_i)_{i\in \mathcal{I}}$ the connected components of $\{s \geq 0 : H(\rho_s)- \inf_{[0,s]}H(\rho)>0\}$ and we write $(\rho^i, W^i,\Lambda^i)_{i\in \mathcal{I}}$ for the associated subtrajectories, then a.s. we have: 
