{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.820709+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56f461b34451d8b3a2ed6987480a692c459bff1a0a9da884492a66e8da13edce","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition uni-SHE of arXiv:2411.09614, 'Moment estimates for the stochastic heat equation on Cartan-Hadamard manifolds'] A process $\mathcal{U}=\{u(t,x); (t,x)\in \mathbb{R}_+\times M\}$ solves equation (equation eq:PAM-mild form of the paper) in the sense of Definition (def of Ito sol of the paper) if and only if for every $(t,x)$ the random variable $u(t,x)$ admits a chaos decomposition (equation eq:chaos expansion of the paper)-(equation eq:fk of the paper), where the family $\{f_k(\cdot, t,x); k\geq1\}$ satisfies 
