{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.735482+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_587f83b07171dd1367b703f8fb011321884ffb9737acc6ca3d97cfcb5467073c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 26 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] If the definition of $\Delta^\partial : \langle \mcT \rangle \to \langle \mcT \rangle \otimes \langle \mcT_1 \rangle$ is extended to trees with a coloured subtree containing the root via
