{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.582319+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6205323520a110e485824a9e5e10c1f6a5ff95e71e05481bcfb17ff5c5eeae52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop intro of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $1<p<2$ and $\varphi(x)=|x|^{-s}$. Then, $(X^a_p,\mathscr W_{gap,p})$ is a complete geodesic metric space. The free energy $\mathcal F_\beta$ is weakly $\lambda$-geodesically convex on $(X^a_p,\mathscr W_{gap,p})$ with $\lambda=\beta a^{-\frac{2-p}{p}}>0$, i.e.\ for $\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1\in X^a_p$ there is a constant speed geodesic $(\mathsf{P}_t)_{t\in[0,1]}$ such that for any $0\leq t \leq 1$
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal F_\beta(\mathsf{P}_t)\leq (1-t) \mathcal F_\beta(\mathsf{P}_0)+t \mathcal F_\beta(\mathsf{P}_1)-\lambda \frac{t(1-t)}{2} \mathscr W_p^2(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1).
