{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.286615+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_698eb663a87b94cc06710d5bd4d85af299541437f9a4026aa39fb440198ad2f7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:rwre of arXiv:2603.22652, 'A cohesive account on the ergodic behaviours and scaling limits of Random Walks in Cooling'] Let $\omega$ be sampled from $\mu$. The \emph{random walk in random environment}
(RWRE) is the Markov chain $Z=(Z_n)_{n\in{\mathbb {N}}_0}$ on ${\mathbb {Z}}$ with transition
kernel
\begin{equation}
P^{\omega}(Z_{n+1}=x+e\mid Z_n=x)=
\begin{cases}
\omega(x), & e=+1,\\
1-\omega(x), & e=-1,
\end{cases}
\qquad x\in{\mathbb {Z}},\ n\in{\mathbb {N}}_0.
\end{equation}
We write $P_x^{\omega}$ for the \emph{quenched} law of $Z$ started at $x$ and
\begin{equation}
P_x^{\mu}(\,\cdot\,):=\int_{(0,1)^{{\mathbb {Z}}}} P_x^{\omega}(\,\cdot\,)\,\mu(d\omega)
\end{equation}
for the corresponding \emph{annealed} law (with expectations $E_x^{\omega}$ and
$E_x^{\mu}$).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.284699+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69b3ded28ec0f181cee6a522b6a6558b8e99fc86d3d76163fe7b9c312d3eb3e1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm cor:smc-jump-chain of arXiv:2604.20629, 'Rates of forgetting for the sequentially Markov coalescent'] Let $K_{\mathrm{SMC}}$ be the jump kernel
