{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.589077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6a624855bc4fbe164f9b50a3e56f04d812febafa3aa15e978b97e7d9be49fa0e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:SaS-rv of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] A real random variable $\xi$ is \emph{symmetric $\alpha$-stable
(S$\alpha$S) with scale $\sigma \geq 0$} if
\begin{equation}

\mathbb{E}\bigl[e^{i\theta\xi}\bigr]
= e^{-\sigma^\alpha|\theta|^\alpha},
\quad \theta \in \mathbb{R},
\end{equation}
for some $\alpha \in (0,2]$. We write $\xi \sim \mathrm{S}\alpha\mathrm{S}(\sigma)$
and define $\|\xi\|_\alpha := \sigma$.","status":"unverified"}

