{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.287891+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c9634935202ff72bcff77e50797117108f3cc2335aad5817061c2350f42a517","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:not:symProb of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] The space $\mathcal{M}_{\kappa, d}$  is the set of probability measures $\nu \in \mathcal{P}((\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa})$ that satisfy the following two properties:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item (Leaf Exchangeability) For any permutation $\tau$ on $\{1, \ldots, \kappa\}$, we have
        \begin{equation}

            \nu(dx_0, dx_{\{1, \ldots, \kappa\}}) = \nu(dx_0, dx_{\{\tau(1), \ldots, \tau(\kappa)\}}).
        \end{equation}
        \item (Edge Symmetry) $\bar{\nu}$ satisfies
        \begin{equation}

            \bar{\nu}(dx_0, dx_1) = \bar{\nu}(dx_1, dx_0).
        \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}
    In addition, given $T \in (0, \infty)$, we define the space $\mathcal{M}_{k,d}^T$ to be the set of measures $\mu \in \mathcal{P}((\mathcal{C}_T^d)^{1 + \kappa})$ such that $\mu_t \in \mathcal{M}_{\kappa, d}$ for all $t\in [0, T]$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.114908+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ca3ced1e9d8b35788cec850fe4fd334d75be76d58b4ce342e0a76ec7bdfc74d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem LM41 of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] Let $X$ be a Borel right process on $(E,d)$ satisfying (AC), (H1a) and (H1b).

Let $B\subset E$ be a nearly Borel set of finite $1$-order capacity. Then for any $\lambda>0$, there exists a unique finite, positive measure $\nu^{(\lambda)}_B$ on $E$ with $\mathrm{supp}[\nu_B^{(\lambda)}]\subset \overline{B}$ such that
\begin{equation}
     p_B^{(\lambda)}(x):=\mathbb{E}^x[\mathrm{e}^{-\lambda \sigma_B}]=\int_E u_\lambda(x,y)\nu_B^{(\lambda)}(\mathrm{d} y),\quad \forall x\in E.
 \end{equation}
In particular, for any $\lambda>0$, 
\[
{\mathbb{P}}^x\left[\sigma_B\le t\right] \ge \emph{Cap}_{(\lambda)}(B)  \inf_{y\in \overline B} \int_0^t \mathrm{e}^{-\lambda s} p(s, x, y)\mathrm{d} s,\quad \forall t>0,x\in E.
\]","status":"unverified"}

