    \qquad\text{and}\qquad
    \sup_{\rho_0\leq\rho<1}\mathbb{E}_{\mu_\rho}e^{\theta_0|\sigma(0)-\rho|}\leq K_0\, .
\end{equation}
Then there is $\rho_+=\rho_+(d,(\mu_\rho))\in[\rho_0,1)$ such that $\mathcal T^{(\rho)}$ contains an infinite nearest-neighbor component almost surely for every $\rho\in(\rho_+,1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

