{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.092498+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e4a95d88d33d7067583dcf00ad3cf2124bff1ba67881d9950b47444a84f7643","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop equation:consistency of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Fix a  continuous function $h:\mathbb{R}_+\to \mathbb{R}_+$ with $\sigma_h \in(0, \infty)$  and  $h(0) = h(\sigma_h) = 0$. There exists  a unique  measure  $\mathbf{Q}^h_{x,r}({\mathrm{d}} \overline{W})$ on $\mathcal{W}_{\overline{E}}^{\mathbb{R}_+}$ such that, for every  $n \geq 1$, $A_0, A_1,  \dots, A_n$ measurable subsets of $\mathcal{W}_{\overline{E}}$ and  $0 = t_0 < t_1 < t_2 \dots < t_n$, we have 
