{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.519505+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6e63853779cc31dc1514813033b425ba51c91769ce958c9faa2d6a45667e5667","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Lower-tail bound for weighted Bernoulli sums) of arXiv:2608.18392, 'On Samuels' Conjecture'] Let $T := \sum_{i=1}^nw_iB_i$, where $B_i\sim\operatorname{Bernoulli}(p_i)$ independently, $0\leq p_i \leq1$ and $0\leq w_i\leq1$. Let $0<a_1\leq\cdots\leq a_n$ satisfy $w_ip_i\leq a_i$. Assume
