{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:36:49.844249+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6ef0ea223cba076964420975a29963ddcbb6ce6c00476bec8b52fdc7b7a2e82a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:weighted-membrane-limit of arXiv:2609.02829, 'Quantitative explosion and percolation of the divisible sandpile'] Let $d\geq5$ and $T>0$, let $q:[0,T]\to\mathbb{R}$ be continuous, and suppose that
