{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.029000+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f7a13e0c69cc0d43669f018a2bb950aea5107d74241fcca45f3ba191cb2ae60","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro 13 of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] Let \( \Omega \subset \R^n \) be an open convex subset and $\phi\in\text{\rm SCL}\,(\Omega)$. For any $x\in\Omega$, the following statements are equivalent.
	\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
		\item $x\in\reg(\phi)$.
		\item $\phi$ is differentiable at $x$, and there exists an open neighborhood \( V \) of \( x \) and $C>0$ such that
		\begin{equation}
			|\phi(y)-\phi(x)-D\phi(x)\cdot(y-x)|\leqslant \frac{C}{2}|y-x|^2,\quad \forall y\in V.
		\end{equation}
		\item $\phi$ is differentiable at $x$, and there exists an open neighborhood \( V \) of \( x \) and $\lambda>0$ such that
		\begin{align*}
			|p-D\phi(x)|\leqslant\lambda|y-x|,\quad \forall y\in V,\ p\in D^+\phi(y).
		\end{align*}
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.660687+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6f8e8635ff34165b4b4b8af36b100ff4d16e26b1ee56bc61d9bf6c8d452c24b1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:CLE4-thin of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $\alpha\in(0, 1)$. Consider $\mathds A_{-2\lambda, 2\lambda}$ in a valid domain $D$ and index its loops by decreasing size of diameter. For any continuous, bounded  function $f:\mathbb C\to\mathbb R$,
