{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.339960+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_703e5e431e39a2a61bbbabf5f084586ec13a4af517a9a195ef70e6698f714067","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma prop:lyap:pdeProp of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] Let $(U, W)$ satisfy Assumption (as:results:lyapunov of the paper). Let $(\mu, \gamma)$ be a linear growth solution to the $\kappa$-MLFE{} on $[0, T]$ with potentials $(U, W)$ and initial condition $\lambda \in \mathcal{Q}_{\kappa, d}$. Recall the definitions of $b$, $g$, and $\eta$ from (equation eq:results:drift of the paper), (equation eq:results:potential of the paper), and (equation eq:not:eta of the paper) respectively, and define
    \begin{equation}
    \bar{\eta}(t, x, y) := \big( \gamma(t, x, y), \gamma(t, y, x) \big), \quad (t, x, y) \in [0, T] \times (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^2.

\end{equation}
Then for almost every $0 \leq r < t < T$, we have
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{split}
        \int_{(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa}}  \Big( \log \mu_t(\mathbf{x})& + g(\mathbf{x}) \Big) \mu_t(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{x} - \int_{(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{1 + \kappa}}  \Big( \log \mu_r(\mathbf{x}) + g(\mathbf{x}) \Big) \mu_r(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{x} \\
