{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.276369+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7076f8780b7bdeaeec49fee40a372bee4ea69f1252290e2f9a51e9502e77044f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 4 (Poisson shape-mixtures of gamma densities need not be HCM) of arXiv:2606.22066, 'A Bessel-zero obstruction to hyperbolic complete monotonicity of noncentral chi-square den'] The class of HCM densities is not closed under Poisson mixing over the gamma shape parameter, even when the rate is fixed.  More precisely, for every \(a,b,\theta>0\),
