    \| \hat{Y}^{x,y}_t\|_{L^p(\hat{\P})} \leq \left\{ e^{-p(\beta  /2) t}|y|^p + C_{\beta,p}^{(1)} \right\}^{1/p} \leq e^{-(\beta  /2) t}|y| + C_{\beta,p}^{(2)}. 
    \end{align*}
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.585031+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_780bd508cfb998275d6c67944884636e9190dc122016018f0d7f50dfabe39d69","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def:metr_pointpr of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] For a monotone configuration $\bar\xi\in\Gamma_m$ recall the enumeration $(\bar\tau_\ell)_{\ell\in\IZ}$ from (equation eq:bartau of the paper). For $(x,y)\in \bar\xi$ with $\bar \tau_\ell(\bar\xi)=(x,y)$ some $\ell\in\IZ$ we denote by $(x^+,y^+)\in \bar\xi$ the point $\bar\tau_{\ell+1}(\bar\xi).$
