{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.122568+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7818dd7c9628059d0c6d69277c9a608959951119bb12a83ba0e879b9f270fd62","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop coro:russeuni of arXiv:2601.20502, 'Optimal matching under size priority'] If $X,X',Y,Y'$ are four real valued random variables such that $X$ is integrable, $Y\overset{\mathcal{L}}{=}Y'$ and $X' \leq 0$ almost surely.
