{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:25:40.343104+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7827c2c6ff76a268935b4661e384836d2d1bef42476ce2b92e60394ae79357e9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:bound on p_u for Voronoi of arXiv:2503.21737, 'High-intensity Voronoi percolation on manifolds'] Assume that $M$ is simply connected and one-ended, has a positive global injectivity radius, and all sectional curvatures of $M$ are bounded from above. Then, for every $\lambda>0$, either $p_c(M,\lambda)=p_u(M,\lambda)> 1/2$ or
