{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.276748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78a30dc7236aedd6d74904c0036fad3bdbfc16057661ccb106f12d02db3cc4d8","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 8 (Signed Bell generating function) of arXiv:2606.22066, 'A Bessel-zero obstruction to hyperbolic complete monotonicity of noncentral chi-square den'] With \(d_m\) as in Proposition~\ref{prop:bell-obstruction},
\begin{equation}

\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}
\mathcal B_n(d_1,\dots,d_n)\frac{z^n}{n!}
=
e^{-bz}F_a(b\theta z).
\end{equation}
Equivalently,
\begin{equation}

\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}
(-1)^n\mathcal B_n(d_1,\dots,d_n)\frac{t^n}{n!}
=
e^{bt}F_a(-b\theta t).
\end{equation}
Moreover, equivalently as an ordinary Taylor expansion,
\begin{equation}

e^{bt}F_a(-b\theta t)
=
\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}
\frac{b^n}{(a)_n}L_n^{(a-1)}(\theta)t^n,
\end{equation}
where \(L_n^{(a-1)}\) denotes the generalized Laguerre polynomial, with normalization
\begin{equation}
L_n^{(a-1)}(\theta)
=
\frac{(a)_n}{n!}\,{}_1F_1(-n;a;\theta).
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}

(-1)^n\mathcal B_n(d_1,\dots,d_n)
=
\frac{n!b^n}{(a)_n}L_n^{(a-1)}(\theta).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.722509+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_790498f4f1ca84b4653b3cfed2b30efd4eb791351c0c0e028c6e2ea4e9809a02","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm5.1' of arXiv:2606.01944, 'Propagation of Chaos for Mean-field Mean Reflected Backward Stochastic Differential Equati'] The reflected BSDE (equation eq7' of the paper) has a unique solution $(\{Y^i,Z^i\}_{1\leq i\leq N},K^{(N)})$ with $K^{(N)}\in \mathcal{A}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)})$, $Y^i\in \mathcal{S}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)})$ and $Z^i\in \mathcal{H}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)};\mathbb{R}^N)$ for $i=1,\cdots,N$. Moreover, there exists a constant $C$ independent of $N$, such that
