\end{equation}
Then, $(\widetilde{w}^{(i)})^{\top}T=2^{-i}(\widetilde{w}^{(i)})^{\top}$. Furthermore, $\langle \widetilde{w}^{(i)}, {w}^{(j)}\rangle=\delta_{i, j}$ for any $i, j\in \mathcal{E}_n$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.788685+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_79538080551f2c7c12668ace0809ab12e38d6db440c5a452765416d3c114af34","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem of arXiv:2606.09228, 'On topological indices of random caterpillar graphs'] We have
