{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.330457+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_79e8b363cc46e9e0cc2c242967f65cabcfb945416570c5e10104525cc108cd33","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:VDC of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] An open set $\Omega\subset\mathbb{G}$ is said to satisfy the \emph{volume density condition} if there exists $c>0$ such that for all $r>0$ and $x\in\partial\Omega$,
