{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.362826+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a28c6d6840fb5e5d95ecfdef3185d0854770650620bea10d5735132d235e098","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2606.18047, 'Analysis of the asymmetric shelf shuffle'] Fix $m\geq 1$ and $p\in (0, 1)$. Let $X(\pi; {\bf x})$ be as in~\eqref{eqn:CycleStructurePoly}. Then,
