{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:35:04.214928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a3427768b504e08bd366570cf9f5676f86a196d5ad6c52acfba82f41a1029aa","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 22 of arXiv:2608.03956, 'From Triangular Array Progression\\ to Near-Log-Concave State Transitions'] Let $\mathcal{S}^{(y,n)}$ be as in (\ref{shannonsum}). Then,
