{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.590037+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7f0e82e11c149f12350c52446aec04b21dfb30100187357f827f9e79fe4c9867","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:kernel of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] For $t, u \in \mathbb{R}$ and parameters satisfying
Assumption~(ass:params of the paper), the \emph{regularized kernel of $n$-MFSM}
is
