        \item[ii)]  The measure $ \mathsf{Q}$ is concentrated on the set of monotone configurations $\bar\xi\in \Gamma_{\IR^2}$.
    \end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.116328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81548918d9e57fbe9916ca25f63859fdd9f4579393391286185a67138d83d1a2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop eq:B2 of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] There exists $p^-_\sigma(\cdot, \cdot,\cdot)\in \mathrm{p} \mathscr{B}((0,\infty))\times \mathscr{B}^*(E)\times \mathscr{B}(E)$ such that 
