$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.580241+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_82911cc718d1dd3ec2b3a7cc0659daa8fb1a768b34f04ba1ee1a140ea2bd2e53","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 ($K_\infty$ is generically not Hilbert--Schmidt) of arXiv:2608.15987, 'Threshold cascades of interacting diffusions on unimodular random trees: a conditional bra'] Let $k_\infty(\xi,\eta)$ be the limiting boundary kernel of the operator programme of Section 1.1, so that $k_\infty(\xi,\eta)\asymp\nu_h(B_{\xi\wedge\eta})^{-\beta}$ for some $\beta>0$ determined by the transmission/Martin exponents, where $\xi\wedge\eta$ is the confluence depth. Then
\begin{align*}
\|K_\infty\|_{\mathrm{HS}}^2&=\iint_{\partial T\times\partial T}|k_\infty(\xi,\eta)|^2\,d\nu_h(\xi)\,d\nu_h(\eta)\\
&\asymp\sum_{n\ge0}\br(T)^{2n\beta}\cdot\nu_h\otimes\nu_h\big(\{|\xi\wedge\eta|=n\}\big)\asymp\sum_{n\ge0}\br(T)^{n(2\beta-1)}
\end{align*}
whenever $2\beta\ge1$ and $g$ is supercritical ($\br(T)>1$). For the Martin-kernel construction one has $\beta\ge1$, since $K(x,\cdot)\asymp\nu_h(B_{|x|})^{-1}$ on the cylinder of $x$ (the Martin kernel is the harmonic-measure density $d\nu_h^x/d\nu_h$). Hence $K_\infty$ is not Hilbert--Schmidt, and the Krein--Rutman route through Hilbert--Schmidt compactness is unavailable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.618254+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_82a8b268bdd4990137b0cdbc72b7b20220bf8931ea79ac2d1bb20fb132823c36","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 38 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Given $k\ge \ell\ge 1$, $\sigma\in(0,1/10)$ and $f\in C_\cc(\R^{\ell})$ let
\begin{equation}

\Xi_k(f):=E\Biggl(f\Bigl(\{X_j+j\slb\}_{j=1}^{\ell}\Bigr)\biggl(\,\prod_{j=1}^{k} \wt P(M_{j}'\le t)|_{t:=X_j+j\slb}\biggr)\,1_{\{X_k\in[k^{\sigma},k^{1-\sigma}]\}}X_k\Biggr),
\end{equation}
where~$X$ is the random walk with step distribution $\NN(0,1/2)$. Let~$\delta\in(0, 1/2)$. Then $\epsilon_{n,k}(u,f)$ defined for each~$u>0$ and $n\ge k$ by
\begin{equation}

E_{Q_{n,u,u}}\Bigl(f\bigl(\{h(x_0)-h(x_j)\}_{j=1}^\ell\bigr)\Bigr)=\frac{4u}n\Xi_k(f)+\frac un\epsilon_{n,k}(u,f)
\end{equation}
obeys
\begin{equation}

\lim_{k\to\infty}\limsup_{n\to\infty}\sup_{n^{\delta}\le u\le n^{1-\delta}}\bigl|\epsilon_{n,k}(u,f)\bigr|=0.
\end{equation}
Moreover, writing $1$ for the constant function equal to~$1$, we have
\begin{equation}

0<\inf_{k\ge1}\Xi_k(1)\le\sup_{k\ge1}\Xi_k(1)<\infty.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.238773+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_82c8bcc656068d362eab288ebec4d107b213bf04aa26711c1c1e901e119ff743","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:cp-upper of arXiv:2607.00731, 'Sharp Asymptotics for the Largest Component in the Subcritical Regime of Preferential Atta'] Let $(d_n)_{n\ge 1}$ be deterministic degree sequences, and write
\(\ell_n = \ell(\mathbf d_n)\), \(D_n = D_{\mathbf d_n}\),
\(\Delta_n = \Delta(\mathbf d_n)\), and \(\phi_n = \phi_{\mathbf d_n}\).

Assume that:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $D_n \Rightarrow D$ for some random variable \(D\) taking values in \(\mathbb Z_{\ge0}\);
\item $Q(d_n)\to 0$;
\item $\mathbb P(D=0)>0$ and $\mathbb P(D=1)>0$;
\item $\mathbb P(D_n=0)>0$ and $\mathbb P(D_n=1)>0$ for all large $n$;
\item $\mu_4(d_n)\le \Delta_n^{1/2}$ and $\Delta_n\le n^{1/6}$ for all large $n$.
\end{enumerate}
Assume further that, for all large $n$, the equation $\phi_n'(\theta)=0$ has a smallest positive solution $\theta_n\in(0,1)$, and define
\begin{equation}
T_n:=\frac{1}{-\log\phi_n(\theta_n)}
\left[
\log n+\frac{3}{2}\log\bigl(-\log\phi_n(\theta_n)\bigr)
-\frac12\log\phi_n''(\theta_n)
+\log\mathbb E\!\left(D_n e^{\theta_n D_n}\right)
\right].
\end{equation}
If $\theta_n\ell_n/T_n\to\infty$, then for every fixed $\delta>0$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb P\bigl(L_1(\mathrm{CM}(d_n))\le (1+\delta)T_n\bigr)\to 1.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:47:01.656933+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_82d3a4b29ffac0fe1b2df3aeb9f38ad2b5e1da8b12738936c848ba63542291d2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 (Overshoot bound) of arXiv:2604.23133, 'High-Precision Framework for Expected Hitting Times Analysis in the Dice-Sum Process'] Assume the setup and notation of Proposition~\ref{prop:square_cutoff}, and let $K = \sqrt{N} \in \mathbb{N}$.  
