{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.369392+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_82f72f6b09bbedd97b512152df4e0c9921fe1c4fff5de16d77b6a2664adc4fd3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:ap1:wp of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] A family of measures $\{\mu_t\}_{t \in [0, T]}$ is a weak solution to (equation eq:ap1:formalPDE of the paper) with drift $f$ and initial condition $\mu_0 \in \mathcal{P}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m)$ if for all $\phi \in C^{2, 1}(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m_T) \cap C(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m \times [0, T))$ such that there exists $R \in (0, \infty)$ such that for all $t \in [0, T]$ and $x \not \in B_R$, we have $\phi_t(x) = 0$,  we have
\begin{equation*}
    \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m} \phi_t(x) \mu_t(dx) = \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^m} \phi_0(x) \mu_0(dx) + \int_0^t \int_{\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d} (\partial_s \phi_s(x) + \Delta _s\phi(x) - f_s(x) \cdot \nabla \phi_s(x) )\mu_s(dx) ds
\end{equation*}
for almost every $t \in [0, T]$. We let $\mu(dt, dx) := \mu_t(dx) dt$ denote such a weak solution.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.240927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8315338b5ef83b11915bbf4309257766fcdf24135204a5af34fa4c174d8ee2fa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:honest-region of arXiv:2608.20295, 'Physical-Support Confidence Sets for Highly Coherent Dictionaries'] Under Assumption~(ass:frozen-shell of the paper) and the calibration coverage condition
in Equation~(equation eq:training-rectangle of the paper), the totalized correspondence
$\widehat{\mathfrak C}_{q,r,s}^{p}$ is measurable, nonempty, and
compact-valued. Uniformly over $\mathfrak P^p_{q,r}(s)$,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb P_{p_\star,\nu_\star,D_\star}^N
\left[
\mathbb P_{\mu_\star,\sigma_\star}^T
\left\{
    \vartheta_\star
    \in
    \widehat{\mathfrak C}_{q,r,s}^{p}
    \mid Y_{1:N}
\right\}
\ge1-\alpha_T
\right]
\ge1-\alpha_D.

\end{equation}
Consequently, by independence of the calibration and deployment experiments,
with
\[
    \alpha
    =
    1-(1-\alpha_D)(1-\alpha_T),
\]
\begin{equation}
\inf_{\xi\in\mathfrak P^p_{q,r}(s)}
\mathbb P_\xi^{N,T}
\left\{
    \vartheta(\xi)
    \in
    \widehat{\mathfrak C}_{q,r,s}^{p}
\right\}
\ge1-\alpha.

\end{equation}

For $N$ above the fixed block threshold of the robust calibration-moment
construction, define
\begin{equation}
\rho_N(s)
=
C\left[
    (s\wedge\epsilon_N)
    +
    \left(s\wedge\frac{\epsilon_N}{s}\right)
    +
    \left(s\wedge\frac{\epsilon_N}{s^2}\right)
\right].

\end{equation}
Any two dictionaries retained by the same nonempty calibration region have
quotient-dictionary distance at most $\rho_N(s)$.  If
$\epsilon_N\le CN^{-1/2}$, then
\begin{equation}
    \rho_N(s)
    \le
    C\left(
        s\wedge\frac{1}{\sqrt N\,s^2}
    \right).

\end{equation}
Below the block threshold, retaining the full compact shell yields the same
order after adjustment of fixed constants.

For every realization,
\begin{align}
\operatorname{diam}_{\mathrm{pr}}
\left(
    \widehat{\mathfrak C}_{q,r,s}^{p}
\right)
\le{}&
C\rho_N(s)
\notag\\
&+
Cs\,
\mathbf 1
\left\{
    2\tau_{T,q}\ge m_S(\rho_N(s))
\right\}
\notag\\
&+
C\,
\mathbf 1
\left\{
    2\tau_{T,q}\ge m_G(\rho_N(s))
\right\}.

\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.590804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8316e3da084db1a08d4169a28416b2db3d0329e1effbcedcc50baf81e870ce95","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop pro:limit_thm_2.2 of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] Recall $\tilde{x}_n(0)=x_n^f$ and suppose $\{x_n^f, n \in \mathbb{N}\}$ fulfils Assumption~(assumpt:2.9 of the paper). Then, it holds 
