{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.045560+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_855e91acb3083d1bd04fdefae1629aa8d5593074583904bc98aa88ee2dceaaa8","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:optimalGaussian of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] Let $\kappa>1$ and set
\begin{equation*}
 h_*=\frac{2}{\sqrt{\kappa+1}},
 \qquad
 \gamma_*=\sqrt{\kappa+1}\,\log\frac{\sqrt\kappa+1}{\sqrt\kappa-1},
\end{equation*}
so that
\begin{equation*}
 \beta_*=e^{-\gamma_*h_*}=\left(\frac{\sqrt\kappa-1}{\sqrt\kappa+1}\right)^2,
 \qquad
 s_*=\frac{h_*^2}{2}(1+\beta_*)=\frac{4}{(\sqrt\kappa+1)^2}.
\end{equation*}
Let $U_H(x)=\frac12x^\top Hx$ on $\mathbb R^d$ with $\mathrm{Id}_d\preceq H\preceq\kappa\mathrm{Id}_d$, and write $Q=Q_{h_*,\gamma_*}^{U_H}$. Then $Q$ has a unique invariant law $\pi_H$, and $\pi_H$ is a centered Gaussian. For every initial state $z\in\mathbb R^d\times\mathbb R^d$,
\begin{equation*}
 \limsup_{n\to\infty}\lVert \delta_zQ^n-\pi_H\rVert_{\mathrm{TV}}^{1/n}
 \le\sqrt{\beta_*}=\frac{\sqrt\kappa-1}{\sqrt\kappa+1},
\end{equation*}
and for suitable $z$ the limit exists and equals $\sqrt{\beta_*}$. Moreover, there are initial states $z,\widetilde z$ with
\begin{equation*}
 \lim_{n\to\infty}\norm{\delta_zQ^n-\delta_{\widetilde z}Q^n}_{\mathrm{TV}}^{1/n}
 =\sqrt{\beta_*}.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.029492+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_855eda305ec2ddef756ccc917f6f864c43bbf1e7e4b9ee625e28789086cb0524","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 18 of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] Let $\phi\in\text{\rm SCL}\,(\T^n)$. We define the function of \emph{degree of regularity} of $\phi$ as
	\begin{align*}
		R_\phi(x)=
		\begin{cases}
			\inf\{\lambda\geqslant0: |p-D\phi(x)|\leqslant\lambda\cdot d(y,x),\forall y\in\T^n, p\in D^+\phi(y)\},&x\in \reg(\phi),\\
			+\infty,&x\in\cut(\phi),
		\end{cases}
	\end{align*}
	and the sub-level set of $R_\phi$ as
	\begin{align*}
		F(\phi,\lambda)=\{x\in\T^n: R_\phi(x)\leqslant\lambda\},\qquad\lambda\geqslant0.
	\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.732571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85942243a059977b21da8bfb411445bd07567e0e1715e7f8ec97809bf9a8dd8c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] Given regularisation scales $0 < \delta < \eps$, throughout this section, we define the smooth and stationary random noise assignment $\tilde{\pi}^{\eps, \delta}: \tilde{\mfL}_- \to C^\infty(\mbR^2)$
	\begin{align*}
		\tilde{\pi}^{\eps, \delta} \<b0> &= \xi_\eps, \quad \tilde{\pi}^{\eps, \delta} \<p0> = \xi_{\delta}, \quad \tilde{\pi}^{\eps, \delta} \<s(1)0> = \eps^{-1/2} \partial_x K \ast \xi_{\eps, \delta}
		\\
		\tilde{\pi}^{\eps, \delta} \<bs(2)0> &= \eps^{-1/2} \partial_x K \ast \xi_{\eps, \delta} \partial_x K \ast \xi_{\eps} - \ell(\<bs(2)0>), \\
		\tilde{\pi}^{\eps, \delta} \<ps(2)0> &= \eps^{-1/2} \partial_x K \ast \xi_{\eps, \delta} \partial_x K \ast \xi_{\delta} - \ell(\<ps(2)0>),
	\end{align*}
	where $\ell(\<bs(2)0>)$ and $\ell(\<ps(2)0>)$ are such that $\mathbb{E}[\tilde{\pi}^{\eps, \delta} \tau(0)] = 0$ for $\tau \in \{\<bs(2)0>, \<ps(2)0>\}$.

	We write $\tilde{Z}^{\eps, \delta} = (\tilde{\Pi}^{\eps, \delta}, \tilde{\Gamma}^{\eps, \delta})$ for the corresponding BPHZ model.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.074433+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_859b8143b87b8055bb570eafa602995a124aaafaaa30506007bd62d78ce014a6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2607.13401, 'Total variation cutoff for Kac's walk on the sphere'] For every \(0\le s_0<\infty\), there are constants
\(\eta_0=\eta_0(s_0)>0\) and \(C=C(s_0)<\infty\) such that the following
holds.  Let \(\alpha,\beta\in\mb R^m\) satisfy
