{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.799333+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_891a5b45e6b3b8443b59f0f67daeffba7ac0138ea7b51ed6f52f5878f8c3a709","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cc-gaussian-flip-probabilities of arXiv:2608.06159, 'Majority Dynamics on Resampled Sparse Erd\H{o}s--R\'enyi Graphs:\\[0.5ex] Gaussian Winner '] Recall \(x_t^{\gR},x_t^{\gB}\) from
    (equation eqn:standardized-degree-difference-definitions of the paper). Fix \(c_0>0\)
    and \(M<\infty\), condition on \(\rvy_t\), and suppose that
    \begin{align}
    |\gR_t|\ge c_0N,
    \qquad
    |\gB_t|\ge c_0N,

    \end{align}
    while $x_t^{\gR}$ and $x_t^{\gB}$ in (equation eqn:standardized-degree-difference-definitions of the paper) satisfy
    \begin{align}
    |x_t^{\gR}|\le M,
    \qquad
    |x_t^{\gB}|\le M.

    \end{align}
    Then, uniformly over such configurations,
    \begin{subequations}
    \begin{align}
    p_t^{\gR}
    &=
