{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.099636+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8ba12d9ade90311ccc219e05afb88e14b3643cc23e6164f17d15f8c3aae0b585","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro Zlawexistencebis of arXiv:2601.20502, 'Optimal matching under size priority'] There is a distribution vector $\mathcal{H}$ such that the law $\zeta'_{\mathcal{H}}$ constructed by Equation~(equation eq:zeta'translation of the paper) on $\mathbb{R}^2$ satisfies the following recursive distributional equation:

