{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.447883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8c12c64673c3e17243bca8ae73faa056222909e59e9436d10425e6390da20a89","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2606.15843, 'Long-time behaviour of DLRA for SDEs'] Suppose that Assumptions (H4), (H5), (H7) and (H8) hold. Moreover, for any $p\ge 2$, suppose $2L_{b,7}-(p-1)L_{\sigma,1}>1$ holds, where $L_{b,7}$ and $L_{\sigma,1}$ are in (H8) and (H3), respectively. Then, for all $t \ge 0$, it holds that 
