{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.700890+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d48ac338bd3141a223faf1f528c8318a3ac393f54ce97151c583954e5445c95","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop basis of arXiv:2609.00672, 'Deciding superellipticity and computing the Weierstrass normal form'] The differential $\omega_{a,b}$ is holomorphic on $C$ if and only if $(a,b)\in A$, where

\begin{equation}
A=\Bigl\{(a,b): a\ge 0,\ 0\le b<n,\ a+\sum_{j}\Bigl\lfloor\frac{b\,l_j}{n}\Bigr\rfloor\le\frac{bm}{n}-1-\frac{1}{e_\infty}\Bigr\}.
\end{equation}

The set $\{\omega_{a,b}\}_{(a,b)\in A}$ is a basis of $H^0(C,\Omega^1)$, and

\begin{equation}
\ord_P(\omega_{a,b})=na+n-1-\bigl(b\,l_i \bmod n\bigr),
\end{equation}

where $b\,l_i\bmod n$ denotes the least non-negative residue.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.857748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d569187253fe6b363cbe5d3ebec098c5d6aeffdb09ba90f01c74f60200279f9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:vvmeasx_weak_conv of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] The sequence of vector measures $(\sigma^{(a,\varepsilon_{n,a})})_{n\in\mathbb{N}} \subseteq \mathrm{ca}(\mathcal{B}(L),H_0^{-1})$ converges weakly to $\sigma^{(a)}$, i.e.
	\begin{equation*}
		\sigma^{(a)} \xleftarrow{\;w\;} \sigma^{(a,\varepsilon_{n,a})} \subseteq (\sigma^{(a,1/n)})_{n\in\mathbb{N}}.
	\end{equation*}
	Moreover, for every $h\inH_0^1$, it holds
	\begin{equation}
		\var{\sigma^{(a)}(h,\cdot)}(\cdot) = |\bar{h}_x|\,\mu^{(a)} (\cdot) \quad \text{and} \quad \var{\sigma^{(a)}}(\cdot) = \|\delta_x\|_{H_0^{-1}} \,\mu^{(a)}(\cdot),
	\end{equation}
	which implies that $\sigma^{(a)}$ is bounded w.r.t.\ $\| \cdot \|$ by $(2\pi a(1-a))^{-1/2}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.041284+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8d7c501f31a5cf959b2c6fc13d727066cfe3db18946f1cc4c13ba458d26757da","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 17 of arXiv:2609.00743, '$L_p$ Brunn-Minkowski inequality for the eigenvalue of generalized Monge-Ampère equation'] For $\Omega_0,\Omega_1\in \mathcal{U}_s$ and $\alpha\in[0,1]$, we have
