{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.551268+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_903832df3cb400198b35b987b207fe371a1cb4a380320074701e341b7eb51f98","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2604.01978, 'Homogenized Transformers'] {\cite[Thm 6.2.1]{vershynin2018high}} 
Suppose $X\in \reals^{n}$ is a random vector with independent, mean-zero, subGaussian coordinates and $B \in \reals^{n\times n}$. Then for every $t\geq 0$, we have
\begin{equation*}
\P\left(\left|X^{\sT}BX-\E\left[X^{\sT}BX\right]\right|\geq t\right)
\leq
