\end{equation}
Consequently, if $h_N(t):=\mathbb E_{N,\delta}r_N(t)^\beta$, then
\begin{equation}
h_N''(0)=\beta(\beta-2\delta)\mathbb E_{N,\delta}r_N'(0)^2.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.705231+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91580d386e0a83233c9b7175dbd2c7010ac51620319cbacf3e2aa4e58288e798","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 4 (Control-law relative entropy) of arXiv:2609.02196, 'Schr\"odinger Bridges on Lie Group Manifolds for Probabilistic Intrinsic Generation'] For controlled laws with the same initial law and diffusion coefficient,
