\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.550641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_923e54303387905389ced97914c9fef794ae3a4f26de7b917ddd7b7463be755c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2604.01978, 'Homogenized Transformers'] Under Assumption \ref{ass:high_order_short}, there exist $C_1,C_2>0$ independent of $\alpha, \eta, L$ such that
\begin{enumerate}
