{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.414370+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9331d30cfb330b861ce2e198df8aae1a61fb2834eccb7b20070ea727fa97094f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor: approx of A from estimate at p-1 of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] For every $\gamma \in (1,2)$, there exists $\bar \varepsilon_\gamma>0$ such that for $(\lambda,C^2) \in S^0$ with $|p-1-\lambda|<\bar \varepsilon_\gamma$ 
