{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.030404+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9337bdc50b84483b2364b2d5e96379542539280ca7607b6555608ab87159bd65","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2606.07096, 'Non-Selection of Lagrangian Trajectories in the Zero-Noise Limit for a Class of Stochastic'] Let $(P_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the Markov semigroup associated to a Lévy process $L$; assume that there exists $M>0$ such that
