obeys
\begin{equation}

\lim_{m\to\infty}\sup_{t,u\ge m} \limsup_{n\to\infty}\,\bigl|\,\epsilon_{n,t,u}\bigr|=0.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.524302+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_939b4788c1b570454c759ddc982a2f9f6031e8c62cf75b18806b7b44c2698b23","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 (Preservation of a common lower bound) of arXiv:2608.18392, 'On Samuels' Conjecture'] Let $\nu_i \in \mathcal{M}(1)$ have the representation in \cref{eq.two_point_mixture} with mixing measure $\eta_i$,
