{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.995778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94db34efae0909e661a58d2512cdc59ce36d159c6cb364c2cede9b6de083d61d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm P typ gau of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] There exist a deterministic constant $c_1\in(0,\infty)$
