{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.048641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96b68daf1ca19759d1876cbdb11202097e915464c1146e6e090e8e26dd3060c7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def-Dmut of arXiv:2506.10448, 'Hitting probabilities and the Ekstr\"om--Persson conjecture'] Let $\mu \in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. For every $t\geq 0$, let 
