{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.239686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97403817adce7fb55797920bf995449e5a6dad15b8eb42e0acb039e5cead6c61","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 61 of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Let \(\mcalM\) be the category of morphisms \(R \to T\) in \(\Perfd\) such that \(R\) is \(p\)-torsion-free and \(T\) is an \(\setF_p\)-algebra.
