{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.750722+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_97bd34dbe70e7f229b16bfd2b8be7a3b0d3add277a3d8856a18320457aa4e770","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:Schauder_est_intr of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] For any $\alpha,\gamma\geq 0 $ and $T>0$, there exists $C=C(\alpha,\gamma,T,B)>0$ such that 
