\frac{1-q}{1-q^n}q^{n-1},\ M=0.\end{cases}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.557464+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a5dbe015209a2e7eace991ef39c9622b16c764e8f94b7b6d0ea154e90351f09","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:first-counter-example of arXiv:2604.04882, 'On a Problem of M. Kac on Laplace Distributions'] The functions
