{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.669330+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d08879b921aa0be5610a977f6f53212c21b2c73326b3a39a53488547085d247","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 (Local asymptotics) of arXiv:2608.04799, '2608.04799'] Fix \(q\ge1\), a surplus vector
\(\mathbf r=(r_1,\ldots,r_q)\in\mathbb Z_{\ge0}^q\), and
\(0<a<b<\infty\).  Let \(k_i=k_i(n)\) range over integers such that
