{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.651360+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a40554aba6f3a6dafc12164cd5ea265793c80b23888f1c95358ab2c147639c0d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 3 (Wigner matrix) of arXiv:2605.07050, 'Universality of the fluctuations of the free energy in generalized Sherrington--Kirkpatric'] A Wigner matrix is an $N \times N$ real symmetric matrix $W$ whose upper triangle entries $W_{ij}$ are i.i.d. real random variables satisfying the following conditions:
\begin{itemize}
\item The entries are centered, i.e., $\E[W_{ij}] = 0$ for all $i, j$.
\item The variances of the entries are normalized so that $\E[W_{ij}^2] = N^{-1}$ for $i \neq j$ and $\E[W_{kk}^2] = w_2 N^{-1}$ for a constant $w_2 \geq 0$.
\item For any integer $s>2$, there exists a constant $C^W_s$ such that $\E[|\sqrt{N} W_{ij}|^s] \leq C^W_s$ for all $i, j$.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.590344+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a40d7dede71e23f14ed3378bf0952ce15362197135ff40e8f0d71825920dec64","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:harmonizable of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] Let $\widetilde{M}_\alpha$ be a complex isotropic S$\alpha$S random
