{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.115260+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a501ea254e51b0f34cc16cb019219b185100ae322fd1ec81eb394e2178303ad7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem LM53 of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] Assume that the Borel right process $X$ satisifes (AC) and (H3'), and that $X$ is transient.  Let $B\in \mathscr{B}^n(E)$ be a nearly Borel set such that $p_B\in {\mathcal{F}}_\mathrm{e}$. Then there exists a unique measure $\nu_B\in \mathscr{M}$ such that ${\mathcal{F}}_\mathrm{e}\subset L^1(E,\nu_B)$ and
