{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:17.979294+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a531f3268b21d1da21e2b66e8a13c9ecc24366bdd1832baa499369d89622ea8d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 19 of arXiv:2507.06186, '2507.06186'] For any $\ka,\eps,t>0$, we let $\mc K_{\ka,\eps}(t)$ denote the integral operator on $L^2(D)$ with kernel
