{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.363384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a56c159d36d433f6d4d61629e47a0cbaf27986e1e0c426aeaafa9e3e9faae446","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 11 (First two descent moments) of arXiv:2606.18047, 'Analysis of the asymmetric shelf shuffle'] Let $n,m\geq 1$, let $\pi\sim\nu_{n,m}^{(p)}$, and let $D_n=\des(\pi)$. Put $\dd=2p-1$. Then
\begin{equation}

\E[D_n]
=
\frac{n-1}{2}
+
\dd\left(
 m-\frac{n+1}{2}
 -\frac{n+1}{m^n}S_n(m)
\right).
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{align}

\E[D_n(D_n+1)]
&=
\frac{n(n+1)}{4}-\frac{m}{2}
+\frac{(n+1)mS_n(m)-(n+2)S_{n+1}(m)}{m^n} \notag\\
&
+\dd\left(
 nm-\frac{n(n+1)}{2}
 -\frac{n(n+1)}{m^n}S_n(m)
\right) \notag\\
&
+\dd^2\left(
 m^2-\left(n+\frac12\right)m+\frac{n(n+1)}{4}\right. \notag\\
&\qquad\left.
 +\frac{(n^2-1)mS_n(m)-n(n+2)S_{n+1}(m)}{m^n}
\right).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.320465+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a584364339fe8460bf49b112f84c62878ed07fb1122b06f798e3468e215e8f69","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2602.11129, 'Information-Theoretic Thresholds for Bipartite Latent-Space Graphs Under Noisy Observation'] Given any $r_1, \ldots, r_k \in \alpha \times \alpha$, set $\gamma \coloneqq {\textsc{Supp}}(r_1, \ldots, r_k)$. Then for any $\beta \subseteq \alpha$ and all $\mathbf{t}$, we have 
