{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:35:05.801627+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5ac98d53adad89985f974f02c372f96181bb4fb973e42c4095d4509888e3029","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:prn_phi of arXiv:2606.23547, 'The location of the largest exponential spacing and Euler’s generalized pentagonal numbers'] For $1\le r\le n$,
