{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.327341+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5b2b17e48f70fd980982058023d573e010bd06f093412bcbae4d20d55d4517b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop mr0 of arXiv:2411.06571, 'Moment-based approach for two erratic KPZ scaling limits'] In the setting of Proposition (mr of the paper), there exists a random four-parameter function $\tilde Z_{s,t}(x,y)$ with $-\infty<s<t<\infty$ and $x,y\in \Bbb R$, H\"older continuous on compact sets of $\{ (s,t,x,y): s<t\}$ and satisfying the following properties: 
    \begin{enumerate}\item $(Z_{s,t},f) = \int_{\Bbb R^2} \tilde Z_{s,t}(x,y)f(x,y)dxdy$ almost surely for all $s,t\in\Bbb Q \;(s<t)$ and all $f\in C_c^\infty(\Bbb R^2)$. In particular, $\tilde Z$ is defined on the same probability space. \item If $(s_j,t_j)$ are disjoint intervals then $\tilde Z_{s_j,t_j} $ are independent.
    \item If $s<t<u$ and $x,z\in\Bbb R$, then we have the a.s. relation 
    \begin{equation}\tilde Z_{s,u}(x,z) = \int_{\Bbb R} \tilde Z_{s,t}(x,y)\tilde Z_{t,u}(y,z)dy.
    \end{equation}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.050754+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5b83ad390251f3ab413c60e76230c66f670d2acd9089d6cfc9ecb26cc62eabc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:LRPseparation of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] For every $R\ge1$ and $n\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 \norm{\delta_{z_R^{\mathrm{cyc}}}Q_R^n-
       \delta_{z_R^0}Q_R^n}_{\mathrm{TV}}
 \ge1-4n\exp\left(-\frac{R^2}{8000}\right).
\end{equation}
Moreover, there is a constant $C<\infty$, independent of $R$, such
that $Q_R$ has a unique invariant law $\pi_R$ satisfying
\begin{equation*}
 \int(\lvert x\rvert^2+\lvert v\rvert^2)\,\pi_R(dx,dv)\le CR^2,
 \qquad R\ge1.
\end{equation*}
Consequently the bound (equation eq:LRPexplicitbound of the paper) holds, proving Corollary~(cor:LRPexplicit of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:37:15.264114+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5eae5f35b1445bdab0bb6ffe739aa51584ce8d5f3a13c005de8fa6d5ca76111","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[2 3 of arXiv:2607.12303, 'Marginal Stationary Distributions and Convergence Rates of Higher Order Markov Chains'] {\rm \cite{HanXu24a}}

