{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.864111+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a6ac313c3ab2e3437b465d1ad600821b95c7c1156c40c98896b10e1929636a88","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 54 of arXiv:2609.03875, 'Measure theory without infinities'] Let $\mf A$ be an HOTM and $\mu$ and $\nu$ be $\mf A$-valued premeasures such that $\q{\mu}=\q{\nu}$. 
