{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.040295+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a745cab3102dbcc8b6251fa5b63209f9cda2db24d138a1137a658e24ac9fbd1b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2606.26619, 'Ergodicity of stochastic reaction-diffusion equations on unbounded domains driven by space'] Suppose that (H2), (H4) and (H5) hold. 
