{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:32:20.751804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b37bf48eb9ad503b57ca42109ffb0729bcc1edb1687ae5e58e8b5c8565cc3aa6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 7 of arXiv:2609.00448, 'Equivariant formality and representation theory'] (\cite[p. 172]{H}, \cite{GD}). Let $A$ be a ring and $B$ an $A$-algebra. The module of K\"ahler differentials $\Omega^1_{B/A}$ of $B$ over $A$ is the quotient of the $B$-module freely generated by the symbols $\{db| b\in B\}$ by the submodule generated by the following sets
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item(Constancy of elements of $A$) $\{da| a\in A\}$, 
		\item(Linearity of $d$) $\{d(b_1+b_2)-db_1-db_2| b_1, b_2\in B\}$, and 
		\item(Derivation) $\{d(b_1b_2)-b_1db_2-b_2db_1| b_1, b_2\in B\}$.
	\end{enumerate}
	The Grothendieck differentials $\Omega^*_{B/A}$ is defined to be the exterior $B$-algebra $\displaystyle\bigoplus_{p=0}^\infty \bigwedge\nolimits_B^p\Omega_{B/A}^1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.615481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b39dab285075b791d637b19afd9c7f58bd2254b2c32b272062e58fdfe2ad8780","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Given a locally-finite random point measure $\eta$ on~$\R$, a Branching Random Walk with step distribution~$\eta$ started at $x\in\R$ is a sequence
$\{\xi_k \}_{k \ge 0}$
of random locally-finite point measures on~$\R$ such that $\xi_0=\delta_x$ a.s.\ and, denoting
$\scrF_k:=\sigma(\xi_j\colon j\le k)$,
\begin{equation}

E\bigl(\texte^{-\langle\xi_{k+1},f\rangle}\,|\,\scrF_k\bigr) =\texte^{-\langle\xi_k,\tilde f\rangle}\quad\text{where}\quad\tilde f(h):=
- \log E \bigl(\texte^{-\langle \eta, f(h+\cdot) \rangle} \bigr)
\end{equation}
holds for all $k\ge0$ and all continuous $f\colon\R\to[0,\infty)$  with compact support.","status":"unverified"}

