{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.532036+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5aeb6f753a33d5f0bf13bcd16a42a9a71ffe69b9fda9eac0cb036bface5c36c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition D:horizon-topology of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Let $L$ be an interval in $\mathbb{R}$ and let $J \in \{\mathbb{R}, \mathbb{Z}\}$, and fix a distinguished point $\gamma_0 \in L$. Define $\mathcal{D}(L, J, \gamma_0)$ to be the set of functions $F:L \times J \to \mathbb{R}$, such that (denoting $F_\gamma(j)=F(\gamma,j)$)
\begin{itemize}[nosep]
    \item $F_{\gamma_0}$ is continuous if $J = \mathbb{R}$;
    \item $F_\gamma(0) = 0$ for all $\gamma$;
    \item there is a $\sigma$-finite measure $\mu_F$ on $L \times J$ such that for any $\gamma_1<\gamma_2\in L$ and $j_1<j_2\in J$, we have
    \begin{equation}

        \mu_F((\gamma_1, \gamma_2] \times ((j_1, j_2]\cap J)) = F(\gamma_1, j_1) + F(\gamma_2, j_2) - F(\gamma_1, j_2) - F(\gamma_2, j_1). 
    \end{equation}
\end{itemize}
We say that $F^n \to F$ in $\mathcal{D}(L, J, \gamma_0)$ if $F^n_{\gamma_0} \to F_{\gamma_0}$ in the uniform-on-compact topology, and $\mu_{F^n} \to \mu_F$ vaguely. This turns $\mathcal{D}(L, J, \gamma_0)$ into a Polish space.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:23:03.034406+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5c2f0342ff42266686019153cea6b995e321db8aff3044550c592c4562974ea","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 19 (Uniform-in-time first Malliavin derivative bounds) of arXiv:2605.03057, 'Uniform-in-time quantitative fluctuations of large scale interacting particle systems'] Let $p\in\left\{4,8\right\}$. Assume
Assumptions~\ref{ass:smooth}, \ref{ass:second-malliavin-uniform}(i),
\ref{ass:coeff-level-new}(i)(ii), and
\ref{ass:first-malliavin-uniform}. Then, there exists a constant
$C_p>0$ such that, for all $N\ge 1$, all $0\le s\le u$, and all
$i,j\in\left\{1,\dots,N\right\}$,
\begin{equation}

\E\left(
\norm{D_s^j X_u^{i,N}}^p
\right)^{1/p}
\le
C_p e^{-\kappa_p \left( u-s \right)/8}
\left(
\mathbf{1}_{\left\{ i=j \right\}}
+
\frac{1}{N}\mathbf{1}_{\left\{ i\ne j \right\}}
\right).
\end{equation}
In particular,
\begin{equation}

\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^N
\E\left(
\norm{D_s^j X_u^{i,N}}^p
\right)^{1/p}
\le
\frac{C_p}{N} e^{-\kappa_p \left( u-s \right)/8}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.849328+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5d011fc5473862df31b98f0eb5d135168e89318c8add2aa2639101861486b7f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 60 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] The following conditions are equivalent:
