{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.650760+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b9210ed8528dcdb830d25d650966b3f9c20444ef62ede436e6cd3f253f422746","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (Regular pre-grazing horizon) of arXiv:2608.16701, 'Order-Sensitive Fast-Synapse Limits in Sparse Excitatory--Inhibitory Threshold--Reset Netw'] A time $T>0$ is regular for the class solution when it is neither a firing
