{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.292244+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c185269e539330303264843119495b0f0634eee34456be158f367cb4e2c1f034","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:beta_perturb of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Fix a (small) $c_0>0$ and a (large) $L>0$. For $w_j=E_j\pm\mathrm{i}\eta_j$ it holds that 
