uniformly in $x_1,x_2\in [c_0,1]$, $x_1\le x_2$, $|z_j|\le L$ and $w_j=E_j\pm\mathrm{i}\eta_j$ with $-L\le E_j\le L$, $0<\eta_j\le L$, $j=1,2$. Here by $\beta_+\beta_-(w_1,w_2)$ we abbreviated the dependence of $\beta_+\beta_-$ on $w_1,w_2$, while the parameters $z_1,z_2$ are the same for both $\beta_+\beta_-$ terms in (equation eq:beta_perturb of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

