{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.859148+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2a4ca4334e1888e12fdb2c4563bb23e92e3ddd1c9405534f3eeff9f667006ff","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm persistence of arXiv:2410.24170, 'Persistent hubs in CMJ branching processes with independent increments and preferential at'] Assume $(X_{j})_{j \in \mathbb{N}}, (X'_{j})_{j \in \mathbb{N}}$ are defined as in~(equation eq:def-ex of the paper) and Assumption~(ass:gen-ass of the paper) is satisfied. Then, in the process $(\mathscr{T}_{\tau_{n}})_{n \in \mathbb{N}_0}$, we have the following: 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item   If the series $\sum_{i=1}^{\infty} (X_{i} - X'_{i})$ diverges almost surely, then, almost surely, $(\mathscr{T}_{\tau_{n}})_{n \in \mathbb{N}_0}$ does not contain a persistent hub.
        \item  Suppose that, for $\alpha > 0$ and $K \in \mathbb{N}$ we have



        \begin{equation} 
