{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.893159+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6bf4449d49ff0decb4e2efe0539dbb60b22c6bbd38815a41a5d1292780b80fd","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2608.26834, 'Small-time annealed large deviations principle for one-dimensional diffusions in a random '] Given a compact set $\mathcal{H} \subset C_0([0,1])$, we have
