{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.863395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6c098652764bbb1b950266aaa4b419ea86f4a94be05e48bc48fd8f8b4fd590c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 49 of arXiv:2609.03875, 'Measure theory without infinities'] Let $\mathbb K$ be an algebraic ring and $\mf A$ be both an HCLM$_{\mathbb{K}}$ and a left $\mathbb K$-module.
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item[(i)]  Let $\mu$ be an $\mf A$-valued measure. If $k\in\mathbb K$ is invertible, then $k\boxdot \mu = k\cdot\mu$.
  \item[(ii)] If $k,l\in\mathbb K$ and $\mu$ is an $\mf A$-valued premeasure, then $(kl)\boxdot\mu=k\boxdot(l\boxdot\mu)$ and $(k+l)\boxdot\mu = (k\boxdot\mu)\boxplus(l\boxdot\mu)$.
  \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.193683+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6f9249383b3348160acf9c6434ffc3ab050b9483b5e28c13091701b4b937e4f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 14 (Generalized resolvent identity) of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] For $H=H^*\in\C^{N\times N}$ and $z_j\in\C\setminus\R$ denote $G_j:=(H-z_j)^{-1}$, $j=1,2$. For any $k,l\in\N$ it holds that
\begin{equation}
G_1^kG_2^l = \sum_{u=1}^k (-1)^{k-u} \binom{l+k-u-1}{l-1} \frac{G_1^u}{(z_1-z_2)^{l+k-u}} + \sum_{v=1}^l (-1)^{l-v} \binom{l+k-v-1}{k-1} \frac{G_2^v}{(z_2-z_1)^{l+k-v}}.

\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.537303+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c6fe05b936444c21e78b6885873083c53141f98fb7de83cc1005ad710f803ea8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem martingale_ineq of arXiv:2411.11759, 'Milstein-type schemes for McKean--Vlasov SDEs driven by Brownian motion and Poisson random'] Let $p\geq 2$. 
