\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.593187+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c72cc7f1f070955a0bf830bf8d9844b38bdc910432d16732f95e961bfb55bf96","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem colour_position_symmetry_step of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] Let $I \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, $\{Z_n\}_{n \in I} \subseteq \mathbb{Z}$ and let $(x^{\textup{step},Z_n}(t),t\geq 0), n \in I,$ be coupled by basic coupling. Then, for any $s \in \mathbb{R}$, it holds
	\begin{equation}
	\mathbb{P} \left( \min_{n \in I} \{ x^{\textup{step},Z_n}_n(T) \} \leq s \right) = \mathbb{P} \left( \min_{n \in I} \{ x^{\textup{step},0}_n(T)+Z_n \} \leq s \right). 
	\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.519716+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7571a266f85b589ccf766118c38d9203acb357b3b023c40c6228e18cd2d6ef3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 (Two-point decomposition) of arXiv:2608.18392, 'On Samuels' Conjecture'] For every $\nu\in \mathcal{M}(1)$, there exists a probability measure $\eta_\nu$ on $\Theta$ such that
