{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.658066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cda5ab51382b224c95fba477133ff9be0c9c987d43eb26908c51a502be1e757c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition a18 of arXiv:2411.19926, 'Sparse Pseudospectral Shattering'] Let $A$ be any random matrix. Fix any $\tau_0 > 0$ and $R > \eta_0 > 0$. Let $\varepsilon = \eta_0/\pare{n\tau_0^{1/2}}$.
