{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.376894+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce2928a5140b8b3457c83f780d1aac594aeab187bbf6a12be226994b5b33dd13","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:potential-identities-results of arXiv:2608.18320, 'Asymptotics for Beta-Splitting Trees via Homogeneous Fragmentations and Meromorphic Potent'] For every $\beta>-2$ and $n\ge2$, the following identities hold.
    \begin{enumeratei}

    \item For every $t\ge0$, the continuous height and the expected total length satisfy
    \begin{equation}
            \mathsf P(D_n>t)=\mathsf E\bigl(F_n(\xi_t)\bigr),
            \qquad
            \mathsf E D_n=\mathcal U_\beta F_n,
            \qquad\text{and}\qquad
            \mathsf E\Lambda_n=\mathcal U_\beta H_n.
    \end{equation}

    \item The expected discrete height satisfies
    \begin{equation}
            \mathsf E L_n=\sum_{j=2}^n a_\beta(n,j),
            \qquad\text{where}\qquad
            a_\beta(n,j)
            =
            \phi_\beta(j-1)\binom{n-1}{j-1}
            \mathcal U_\beta G_{n,j}.
    \end{equation}

    \item Let $M_{n-1}$ be the maximum of $n-1$ independent exponential random
    variables of rate $1$, independent of $\xi$. Then
    \begin{equation}
            D_n\stackrel{d}=T_{M_{n-1}},
            \qquad\text{where}\qquad
            T_x:=\inf\{t\ge0:\xi_t\ge x\}.
    \end{equation}

    \end{enumeratei} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.194064+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce2b3d90fb0177f9baeb0ab8d0cd34b4cac3e2bdc3a0b58a1a6259226d8f5779","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] For any fixed $n,S\in\N$ it holds that
