{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:27:14.873732+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce90e175832969e74cd43719258779d178e092c89572d921bd2f0225018dce46","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2608.23462, '2608.23462'] Let $\beta >0$ and $p \geq 2$. Suppose that Assumptions~\ref{assu:regularity} and~\ref{assu:epsilon} are satisfied and that the fast variable $(Y_t)_{t \ge 0}$ with initial condition $y \in \R^{d_2}$ is $p$-dissipative with constant $\beta$. Then, there exists $C_{\beta,p}^{(1)}, C_{\beta,p}^{(2)} > 0$ such that for all $t\geq 0$
    \begin{align*}
    \| Y_t\|_{L^p} \leq ( e^{-p(\beta  /2) \chi(t)}|y|^p + C_{\beta,p}^{(1)} )^{1/p} \leq e^{-(\beta  /2) \chi(t)}|y| + C_{\beta,p}^{(2)}.
