{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.331118+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce93454e2a8d82909b75af7afe29db2f9a4d7d80f8821a2e849a7b83473669e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:frac_per_bound of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\Omega$ be any measurable subset of $\mathbb{G}$. Then for all $0<\alpha<1$,
    \begin{align}
        \operatorname{Per}^{(\alpha)}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)\leqslant C_\alpha \operatorname{Vol}(\Omega)^{1-\alpha} \operatorname{Per}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)^\alpha
    \end{align}
    with 
    \begin{align*}
        C_\alpha=\frac{\left(2Q\right)^{\frac{\alpha}{2}}}{(1-\alpha)\Gamma(1-\frac{\alpha}{2})} ,
    \end{align*}
    where $Q$ is the homogeneous dimension of $\mathbb G$, and $m$ is the dimension of the first layer of the Lie algebra $\mathfrak{g}$.
     As a result, $\operatorname{Per}^{(\alpha)}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)<\infty$ for all $\alpha\in (0,1)$ whenever $\operatorname{Vol}(\Omega)<\infty$ and $\operatorname{Per}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)<\infty$. In particular, when $\Omega$ is bounded with a $C^1$ boundary, $\operatorname{Per}^{(\alpha)}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)<\infty$ for all $\alpha\in (0,1)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.583084+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce9882b6d592a1c8fe7d388723504e261de8efe03f864d4eb9af8090d197b1fd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi def:cpls of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] For two stationary probability measures $\Pi_i\in \mathcal P_{s,1}( \mathsf{S})$, $i=0,1$ we denote by $ \mathsf{Cpl}_s(\Pi_0,\Pi_1)$ the set of all couplings of $\Pi_0$ and $\Pi_1$, which are invariant under the diagonal shifts 
    \begin{align*}
         \mathsf{S}^2 \ni ( \mathsf{s}, \mathsf{s}')\mapsto (\sigma^ks,\sigma^ks')\in 
         \mathsf{S}^2,\quad k\in \IZ.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:04:39.208906+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ce9a89263995b566817adc4d63519742dc6a0cb9f26fa3bcaa5dff1cc2cbbb16","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2608.13677, 'Asymptotically complete free-energy dissipation: \\ a coarse MLSI holds at any positive te'] \label[lemma]{lemma:computation_flip_density}
    Suppose \(\sigma(\mu) < \infty\), or even just \(\mu \ll \mu \circ \mathrm{flip}_0^{-1}\) (or, equivalently, \(\mu \circ \mathrm{flip}_0^{-1} \ll \mu\)).
    Then, for \(\mu\)-a.e. \(\eta\) and all \(x \in \Lambda_n\), we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{\d \mu_{\Lambda_n \vert \Lambda_n^c}(\cdot \vert \eta) }{\d (\mu_{\Lambda_n \vert \Lambda_n^c}(\cdot \vert \eta) \circ \mathrm{flip}_x^{-1})}(\eta_{\Lambda_n})
        = \frac{\mathrm{d}\mu}{\mathrm{d}(\mu \circ \mathrm{flip}_0^{-1})}(\theta_{x}\eta),
    \end{align*} where \(\theta_x\) means translation by \(x\), i.e., \((\theta_x \eta)_y = \eta_{y+x}\) for all \(y \in \Z^d\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.677729+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cea32ad762368f9dd5f0eaa9fa8e99907ab8d8890107dc4a32bbdae02aeeb837","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 25 of arXiv:2608.30875, 'A Decomposition Theorem for Topological Semi-small Maps'] Let $f : X \longrightarrow Y$ be an almost covering such that $X$ and the fibered set $R$ are closed topological manifolds, and $Y$ is a closed topological $n$-pseudomanifold. Assume that the restriction $f|_{f^{-1}(R)} : f^{-1}(R) \longrightarrow R$ is a fiber bundle with fiber $F$, a closed orientable topological manifold, and that $\operatorname{codim}_{X}(f^{-1}(R)) \geq 2$. Let $\overline{p} \in \{\overline{n}, \overline{m} \}$ be a perversity. Moreover,
      	\begin{enumerate}
      		\item suppose that the normal bundle of $B:=f^{-1}(R)$ exists and is orientable, and that for each $r \in R$ there is a trivializing neighborhood $U$ of $r$ such that the connecting homomorphism in the Gysin sequence of the normal bundle of $B$ restricted to $f^{-1}(U)$ vanishes in degree $\operatorname{codim}_{X}(B)-1$.
      		\end{enumerate}
      		Let $R(f\vert_{X \setminus B})_{\ast}\underline{\mathbb{Q}}_{X \setminus B} \simeq \underline{\mathbb{Q}}_{Y \setminus R} \oplus \mathcal{L}$, where $\mathcal{L}$ is the local system on $Y \setminus R$ induced by the covering map $f\vert_{X \setminus B}$. If $\overline{p}(\operatorname{codim}_{Y}(R))+1 = \operatorname{codim}_{X}(B)$ and $\operatorname{codim}_{Y}(R)$ is even, then
      	\begin{align}
      		Rf_{\ast}\underline{\mathbb{Q}}_{X}[n] \simeq h_{\ast} \big((R^{0}f\vert_{B})_{\ast} \underline{\mathbb{Q}}_{B}[\dim(B)]\big) \oplus IC^{\overline{p}}_{Y} (\underline{\mathbb{Q}}_{Y \setminus R} \oplus \mathcal{L}),
      	\end{align}
      	where $h: R\hookrightarrow Y$ is the inclusion, and $IC^{\overline{p}}_{Y}$ is Deligne's sheaf complex with respect to the stratification $Y \supset R$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.321975+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ced87455ca23e6a5594540197ac34cb8ff3f972c6889429dd75e2fa01bc65765","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary main global corollary of arXiv:2606.01683, 'Singular-value gap of nonreversible Markov processes'] Assume the global singular-value gap $\gamma$ defined in (equation gap definition continuous time of the paper) 
