{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.292015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cef521ab21278a2f6093c15d70606d5ec7b81b3c32689aa03d7c6c593ecb9f32","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary prop:cooling-scgf of arXiv:2603.22652, 'A cohesive account on the ergodic behaviours and scaling limits of Random Walks in Cooling'] {Consider a cooling map $\tau$ as in (equation effective-cooling of the paper) and an environment law $\mu$ as in (equation eq:mu_iid of the paper). Let $X = (X_n, n \in {\mathbb {Z}}_+)$ be the annealed RWCRE obtained from $P^{ \mu, \tau}_0$ as defined in (equation eq:annealed_rwcre of the paper),} and for each $\theta \in {\mathbb {R}}$ let $I^*(\theta): = \lim_{T \to \infty} \frac{1}{T} \log {\mathbb {E}}[e^{\theta Z_T}]$, where $Z = (Z_n, n \in {\mathbb {Z}}_+)$ is the RWRE obtained from $P^\mu$ as defined in (equation eq:annealed_rwre of the paper). Then  
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
        \lim_n \frac{1}{n} \log {\mathbb {E}}[e^{\theta X_n}]&= \lim_n \sum_k \frac{T_{k,n}}{n} \frac{1}{T_{k,n}} \log {\mathbb {E}}[e^{\theta Z_{T_{k,n}}}] = I^*(\theta).
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
{In particular, under the annealed measures, the empirical speeds of RWRE and RWCRE satisfy the same rate $n$ LDP with rate function given by the Legendre-Fenchel transform of $I^*$.}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.855015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cf02479d561a738327b377ca336c805060a5bca015e58266154ab201cb24dea0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem RLD_rec of arXiv:2607.12061, 'Models for species evolution with random deaths'] Let $f^\ddagger_c = \frac{qr}{p-q(1-r)}$ and suppose $p>q$. 
    \begin{itemize}
        \item[(i)] If $f<f^\ddagger_c$, then $|\mathcal{B}(f)|=\infty$ a.s. and $\mathbb{E}[B_{i+1} - B_i] < \frac{f^\ddagger_c}{f^\ddagger_c-f}$ for all $i$.
        \item[(ii)] If $f=f^\ddagger_c$, then $|\mathcal{B}(f)|=\infty$ a.s.
