{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:25:06.156126+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d09a533ca47e561a8eada1b92b37dc419b84e642e1c1debc288fb4eb3e0ca59e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2608.22534, 'Entropy power inequalities in compact groups'] Let $G$ be a connected compact abelian group, let $\mu$ be its 
Haar probability measure and $Y$ be a random variable on $G$ with 
density $f_Y$. Let $S$ be a set of positive Haar measure 
and $g_S = \frac{1}{\mu(S)}\mathbb{I}_S$ be the density of a uniform 
random variable $U_S$ on $S$. For $t>0$, also define
    \begin{equation*} 
    g^t(y) = \frac{t+f_Y(y)}{1+t}, \quad y \in G.
    \end{equation*}
    Then, for all $t > 0 $
\begin{equation*} 
    \chi^2(f_Y \ast g_S \| g^t  \ast g_S) \leq \eta_S\frac{t+\|f_Y\|_{\infty}}{t}\chi^2(f_Y\|g^t),
\end{equation*}
where
$$\eta_S = \left(\frac{\sin(\pi \mu(S))}{\pi \mu(S)}\right)^2.$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.285305+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d0b1cb882d887644f6aa624f2a7c2643e2a7c805b12e07e04fc9345c3406254d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem annealed of arXiv:2604.20660, 'The Legendre structure of the TAP complexity\\ for the Ising spin glass'] Let $f\in\mathbb{R}$, $u\in(0,1)$, $q\in(0,1)$, and
		$\zeta\in\mathrm{Prefix}_2(u,q)$.
		Assume:
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item[\emph{(i)}]
			\emph{(Tail optimality.)}
			$\zeta$ minimizes $\mathcal{P}\mathrm{arisi}$ over $\mathrm{Prefix}_2(u,q)$.
			\item[\emph{(ii)}]
			\emph{(Stationarity.)}
			$(u,q)$ is a critical point of
			$(u',q')\mapsto u'\!\left(\inf_{\zeta'\in\mathrm{Prefix}_2(u',q')}\mathcal{P}\mathrm{arisi}(\zeta')-f\right)$.
		\end{enumerate}
		Let $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$ and let $\mathcal{N}_\varepsilon(f,\zeta)$ be the number of
