{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.050460+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dd2d6f688f8c4420e40810be1066367289c8a822ef570e0fdb02c7a3f0d648ef","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:LRPcycle of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] The deterministic recurrence
\begin{equation*}
 x_{k+1}=\frac{13}{9}x_k-\frac49x_{k-1}-\frac19U'(x_k)
\end{equation*}
has the period-three orbit $(p_k)$. Consider the perturbed recurrence
\begin{equation*}
 x_{k+1}
 =\frac{13}{9}x_k-\frac49x_{k-1}-\frac19U'(x_k)+\varepsilon_{k+1},
 \qquad x_{-1}=p_{-1},\quad x_0=p_0,
\end{equation*}
and set $e_k=x_k-p_k$. Suppose that $x_k$ and $p_k$ lie in the same
interval of (equation eq:Upieces of the paper) for every $0\le k\le n-1$. Then, for
$0\le k\le n-1$,
\begin{equation}
 e_{k+1}=-\frac43e_k-\frac49e_{k-1}+\varepsilon_{k+1},
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \max_{0\le k\le n}\lvert e_k\rvert
 \le9\max_{1\le j\le n}\lvert \varepsilon_j\rvert.
\end{equation}
In particular, if
$\max_{1\le j\le n}\lvert \varepsilon_j\rvert\le1/180$, then
$\lvert e_k\rvert\le1/20$ for every $0\le k\le n$, and $x_k$ and $p_k$
lie in the same interval of (equation eq:Upieces of the paper) at every such step.","status":"unverified"}

