{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.819784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_debad811d5fa4d240a449ce56a8e358f0a20b81b305e426e67bec2f9432846ac","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: Heat Kernel Bound of arXiv:2411.09614, 'Moment estimates for the stochastic heat equation on Cartan-Hadamard manifolds'] Let $M$ be a Hadamard manifold.

    Suppose $t>0,x,y\in M$. If $\sec_M\leq -K_1<0$, the heat kernel $P_t(x,y)$ satisfies \begin{equation}
      P_t(x,y)\leq C h(K_1t,\sqrt{K_1}d(x,y))
    \end{equation}
    where $C>0$ depends on $n$ and $K_1$. Similarly, if $\sec_M\geq-K_2>-\infty$, we have \begin{equation}
        P_t(x,y)\geq ch(K_2t,\sqrt{K_2}d(x,y))
    \end{equation}
    where $c>0$ depends on $n$ and $K_2$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:10.807051+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ded5fdf55553d1de4bc498a5fbbf88271e65ac43bf8005be91e4ab32e9773024","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] Let $0<a\le b<1$ and $A=[a,b]$. For any $n\ge 0$ and any real numbers $0=s_0< s_1 < s_2 < s_n<t=s_{n+1}$, conditionally to the event $\{ e_1^\varepsilon \ge t\}$, the random vector
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
\big( N^\varepsilon_{(s_i, s_{i+1}]} (A)  \big)_{0 \le i \le n}
\end{split}
\end{equation}
converges in law, as $\varepsilon$ goes to $0$, to the random vector 
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
\big( {\bar N}_{i} \big)_{0 \le i \le n}
\end{split}
\end{equation}
composed of independent random variables such that for any $i \in \{0,\ldots, n\}$, $N_i$ is a Poisson random variable with parameter $(s_{i+1} -s_i) \lambda_* (A)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.590544+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dee7d1a017b89fd060100d4ae0b5b735a8865fedc4191dcf6b3e8c15f89ec9b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:LASS of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] Let $X^{(n)}_H$ be an $n$-MFSM satisfying Assumption~(ass:params of the paper)
with $H \in \mathcal{C}^n(\mathbb{R})$ (i.e., $H$ is $n$-times continuously
differentiable; for $n=1$ this is equivalent to $\beta > 1$).
Then for each $t_0 \in \mathbb{R}$:
\begin{equation}

\left\{
\frac{X^{(n)}_H(t_0 + \varepsilon\tau)
  - \displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\frac{X^{(n,k)}_H(t_0)}{k!}\,
  (\varepsilon\tau)^k}
{\varepsilon^{H(t_0)}}
\right\}_{\tau \in \mathbb{R}}
\overset{\mathrm{f.d.d.}}{\longrightarrow}
\bigl\{Y^{(n)}_{H(t_0)}(\tau)\bigr\}_{\tau \in \mathbb{R}}
\quad \text{as } \varepsilon \to 0^+,
\end{equation}
where $Y^{(n)}_{H(t_0)}$ is an $n$-FSM (in the sense of [Kawai2016])
with constant Hurst parameter $H(t_0)$ and stability index $\alpha$,
whose moving-average representation is
\begin{equation}

Y^{(n)}_{H(t_0)}(\tau)
= \int_\mathbb{R}
\frac{(\tau-u)_+^{H(t_0)-1/\alpha}}{\Gamma(H(t_0)+1-1/\alpha)}
\,dM_\alpha(u).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.537592+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df100e587754f62edbe4af1d740d3e403c4164a5cf9a500212b11640901d3062","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem dif:scm of arXiv:2411.11759, 'Milstein-type schemes for McKean--Vlasov SDEs driven by Brownian motion and Poisson random'] If Assumptions     \mbox{\normalfont  (asump:tame of the paper)} to \mbox{\normalfont  (asump:sig:gam:tame of the paper)}   are satisfied, then for any $p_0\geq 2$, $t\in[0,T]$ and $i\in\{1,\ldots,N\}$
