{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.587654+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1d022ecc9131ec208e4fee4ed1977737bf2d453c2b3c80fcad25bd4c8e99c2a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm strictly_smaller_free_energy of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] For $\mathsf{P}_i\in  \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ with  $\mathcal F_{\beta}({\mathsf{P}_i})<\infty$, $i=0,1$, there exists $ \mathsf{Q}\in  \mathsf{Cpl}_{s,m}(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)$ with \begin{align}  
    \mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{t})\leq  (1-t)\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{0})+t\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{1})-\frac{(1-t)t\beta}{2}\int \sum_{(0,0)\neq (x,y)\in \bar\xi} (x-y)^2\inf_{z\in [x,y]}f(\left\lvertz\right\rvert) \mathsf{Q}^0(d\bar\xi),
    \end{align}
     where  $\mathsf U:=\iota( \mathsf{Q})$,  $\mathsf{P}_t:= \mathsf{gap}^{-1}\left((T_t)_{\#}\mathsf U\right)$ and $f$ is chosen as in (equation eq:function_f of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.964361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e1eca934d64eacc7d3934b4ad446fd6b55d54bdcf91d895cbb52d7471d9a1baf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Random Walk of arXiv:2606.14895, 'Effective Resistances and Commute Times in Sparse Random Geometric Graphs'] A random sequence $X_1, ..., X_k$ of vertices in $G$ is a random walk if independently for all $i \in [k-1]$:
\begin{equation*}
    \Pr\left(X_{i+1} = v \mid X_i = u\right) = 
    \begin{cases} 
        \frac{w_{(u,v)}}{\deg(u)} & \text{if } (u,v) \in E\,, \\
        0 & \text{otherwise}.
    \end{cases}
\end{equation*}
Furthermore, let $\mathbf{W} = \mathbf{A}\mathbf{D}^{-1}$ so that 
$\mathbf{W}_{vu} = \Pr\left(X_{i+1} = v \mid X_i = u\right)$. Then
$\mathbf{W}\vec{\mathbf{1}}_u$ is the distribution of vertex locations after one step of a random walk starting from $u$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.730635+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e2257c30bb9e5a6df68c10cde70a4753ac91fe141bee8b31ab995213695417f1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem estimate of arXiv:2503.22334, 'Probabilistic analysis of optimal multi-pivot QuickSort'] For all $0 \le L<\infty$ exists an $M_L<\infty$ such that for all $\lambda \in [-L,L]$ and all $n \ge 0$ we have
