{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.854389+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e735ca06ecf990c854134cdc82a86c08b554307669258d91ba3f2a4642783da0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:l_and_bb_pin of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] Let $x \in (0,1)$, and let $l^x \in C_0$ be defined by
	\begin{equation*}
		l^x_{\xi} \coloneqq \frac{\xi}{x} \, \mathds{1}_{[0,x]}(\xi) + \frac{1-\xi}{1-x} \, \mathds{1}_{(x,1]}(\xi), \quad \xi \in [0,1].
	\end{equation*}
	Consequently, we define the stochastic process $\beta^{\mathrm{pin},x} \coloneqq \big(\beta_{\xi} - \beta_x  l_{\xi}^x \big)_{\xi \in [0,1]}$. Note that the paths of $\beta^{\mathrm{pin},x}$ are in $C_0$, and we have $\beta^{\mathrm{pin},x}_x = 0$ by construction.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.655804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7789eba9bdcd0ad9bd1acb072025a6e1d988ea9a9f1f4ee2a0034a8ace722f2","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 9 of arXiv:2607.24561, 'Range convergence and sharp one-arm asymptotics\\for the critical percolation cluster in h'] Let $\Lambda>3$. There exists a $\Lambda$-dependent constant $C_{\Lambda}$ such that, for all $z \in Q_{0,\Lambda r}\setminus Q_{0,3r}$ and every $\varepsilon>0$, $i \in \{1, \cdots, \varepsilon^{-1}\}$ and $\alpha>0$,
\begin{align*}
       \bP[X_{r,i}\le \alpha r^2| 0 \leftrightarrow Q_{z,r}]\le C_{\Lambda} \frac{\alpha}{(i\varepsilon)^2}.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.300814+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e797778c60a34d0c928743fe92042b1b46551613e98080bb55ac26b790945313","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 3476 of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $ c, q \in (0,\infty) $, $ \beta \in [ \nicefrac{ 1 }{ 2 }, 1 ) $,
let $ \mathcal V \subseteq {\mathbb R}^d $ be measurable, and
let $ ( X, U ) $ be $ ( c, q ) $-regular on $ \mathcal V $ in the sense of (def:regular of the paper).
Consider the stopping time
\bas{
  \bar\tau =
  \inf\bigl\{
    n \in {\mathbb N}_0 \colon \theta_n\not\in \mathcal V
  \bigr\}
  \qquad
  \text{and}
  \qquad
  \sigma^{ (i) } =
  \inf\bigl\{
    n \in {\mathbb N} \colon v_n^{ (i) } \ge \tfrac{ c ( 1 - e^{ - 1 / 2 } ) }{ 2 }
  \bigr\} .
}
Then for all $ n \in {\mathbb N} $ one has
\bas{
  {\mathbb P}\bigl(
    \bar \tau \ge n, \sigma^{(i)} > n
  \bigr)
  \le
  \exp\Bigl(
    - \frac{ q n ( 1 - e^{ - 1 / 2 } ) }{ 4 }
  \Bigr)
  .
}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.872336+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e7d537ef70fdec73f8663a65257ad6f62ec1865d76c6707087e3dabe1bf6e85c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:stima_HS_1 of arXiv:2605.07832, 'A Bismut -Elworthy formula for BSDEs with degenerate noise'] Assume that there exists a positive constant $\delta$ such that 
