{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.334029+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e80ffe7eb254edd67bfbaeb5549724fbaf101e9f71dcfc2f96312cdf50531a1f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop cv explo unif of arXiv:2609.04138, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ I:\\ subsequential limits of the non-simple C'] For all $y \in \BQ^2$, let $C^{\kappa_n}_t(y)$ be the connected component of $\BD \setminus \SCB^{\kappa_n, \partial}_{\ka_{\kappa_n}t}(\partial \BD)$ containing $y$ when it exists and the empty set otherwise (these components are simply connected, $\SCB^{\kappa_n, \partial}_{\ka_{\kappa_n}t}(\partial \BD)$ being a connected closed subset of $\overline{\BD}$ containing $\partial \BD$). Then, jointly with the convergence~(equation eq cv subsequence of the paper), we have
	\begin{equation}
        (C^{\kappa_n}_t(y))_{t \in \BQ_{\ge 0}, y \in \BQ^2}
        \mathop{\longrightarrow}\limits_{n\to \infty}^{(\mathrm{d})}
		(C_t(y))_{t \in \BQ_{\ge 0}, y \in \BQ^2}
	\end{equation}
	for the product topology where the space of simply connected domains containing $y$ is equipped with the Carath\'eodory topology viewed from $y$, to which we adjoin $\emptyset$ as the limit of domains whose conformal radius seen from $y$ tends to $0$, 
	where ${C_t(y)}$ is the connected component of $\BD \setminus \SCB_t^\partial(\partial \BD)$ containing $y$, and where $(\SCB_t^\partial(\partial \BD))_{t\ge 0}$ is the explored region at time $t$ in the uniform exploration of the $\CLE_4$ (denoted $\SCB_t(\partial \BD)$ in~(subsec:labeled_cle_4 of the paper)) (where the time parametrization is that of the PPP of SLE bubbles). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:44:17.187726+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e81627afbd21660645c86957d499a6a5b256b44111722444c56d39fe0eb98f95","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 of arXiv:2604.18871, 'Quantitative approximation of the Vlasov(--Fokker--Planck)--Navier--Stokes system by stoch'] Let Assumption~\ref{assump-particles} hold.
For $k$ as in Assumption~\ref{assump-particles}\ref{hyp:F0Nk} and for any cut-off $A>0$ from \eqref{def:cutoff}, there exists $C = C(T,A,k,d)>0$ such that

