{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.893284+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e82d34344382bf633857ace484f0f3db150b1f943b89fcf307207f55ec773454","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 22 (Environment--partition identification) of arXiv:2608.26834, 'Small-time annealed large deviations principle for one-dimensional diffusions in a random '] Assume $H_4$. If $F\subset C_0([0,1];\R)$ is compact, then
