{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:35:19.876112+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e98c5d451f6691b286236560fa147b0264bae8b89370657233b6c2aafac7bc51","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem stat of arXiv:2608.27939, 'Entropy and domination for quasi-Hitchin representations'] Let $\rho,\sigma:\pi_1(S)\to\mathrm{PSL}_n(\mathbb{C})$ be two representations, and suppose there exist constants $0<\alpha<1$ and $0<\lambda<1$ such that, for all sufficiently large $L$, the ratio
