{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.423288+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb06545466dcd1f1fe686014e19c62f6f1c9975592a0e2cfd8ebd67f70dc3f2a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:En-fg of arXiv:2607.22156, 'A random matrix approach to lamplighter groups'] For $f\in L$, we denote $\mathrm{diam}(f):=\inf\left\{n\in\mathbb{N}:\\supp(f)\subset\llbracket -n,n\rrbracket\right\}$, and $\mathrm{diam}(e_{L})=0.$ For $n\geq0$, we define $\mathcal E_{n}:=\operatorname{span}\left\{U_{f,g}:\\mathrm{diam}(f)\leq n,\ |g|\leq n\right\}.$ We then have
    \begin{equation*}
