{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:33.535357+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebde9abd786c6616c4176f5e0ee877a61734096962d645b25a287034e5e3d5cc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2603.28170, 'Stabilization time of finite configurations with a second class particle in discrete TASEP'] Let $p=\frac{1}{2}-\frac{\lambda}{2\sqrt{n}}$ for some $\lambda\in\R$ be fixed
and let $\omega\in\Omega_n$ be sampled according to the Bernoulli initial condition of parameter $p$ with a second class particle in uniform position.
Then we have that
\begin{equation}
E_n\stackrel\d\Longrightarrow X^{(\lambda)}
\end{equation}
as $n\to\infty$ where the distribution of $X^{(\lambda)}$ is given by
\begin{equation}
\P(X^{(\lambda)}=0)=1-\P(X^{(\lambda)}=1)=\E(\argmax_{s\in[0,1]}B_s^{(\lambda)})
\end{equation}
with a Brownian motion $B_s^{(\lambda)}$ with drift $\lambda$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:44.553817+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebded23b8ecfb5104ecaf478123407a22f9564eea3b72d9ac95c55793ae3bbf2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 15 of arXiv:2604.02129, 'Realisation of constraints in underdamped Langevin dynamics'] The probability measure $\mu^\eps\in \mathcal P(\R^{2d})$ defined in~\eqref{eq:SpatPreLimSte} converges weakly to $\mu\in \mathcal P(\xi^{-1}(0)\times\R^d)$ given by 
\begin{align*}
    d\mu(q^2,p)\coloneqq \frac{1}{Z} \exp\biggl(-V(0,q^2) -\frac{|p|^2}{2}\biggr) dq^2 dp
\end{align*}
where $Z$ is the normalisation constant. 
In particular, for $f\in C_b(\R^d)$ with $f=f(q)$ we have
\begin{align*}
    \lim_{\eps\to 0} \int_{\R^{2d}}f(q)d\mu^\eps(q,p) = \int_{\R^{d-k}} f(0,q^2) \frac{1}{\hat Z} e^{-V(0,q^2)}dq^2,
\end{align*}
with $\hat Z\coloneqq \int_{\R^{d-k}}e^{-V(0,q^2)}dq^2$. 

Furthermore, the limit~\eqref{eq:limit-gen} of $(Q^2,P^2)$ with $\hat q=0$  admits the $(q^2,p^2)$-marginal of $\mu$, i.e.\ $\displaystyle\int_{\R^k}\mu\,dp^1$, as a steady state (cf.Proposition~\ref{prop:Behav-Q2P2}).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.560950+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebe064db40c26cfd4af0088d6bd811b9dc2fafa7f793c161e6f75fa17caf948f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 3.3 of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Let $\tau$ be a finite stopping time, i.e., $P(\tau<+\infty)=1$, and let $\rho,\mu\in{\mathbb R}$ and $\nu\in{\mathbb R}_+$ be three given constants satisfying $\rho> \mu+\frac{1}{2}\nu^2$. Assume that the generator $g$ satisfies
\begin{enumerate}
\renewcommand{(A3)}{(H1c)}
\renewcommand{(A3)}{(A3)}
\item $\displaystyle \mathbb{E}\left[\int_0^\tau e^{2\rho s} |g(s,0,0)|^2{\rm d}s\right]<+\infty$
\end{enumerate}
and assumptions (A:H2 of the paper)-(A:H5 of the paper) with $\mu_\cdot\equiv \mu$ and $\nu_\cdot\equiv \nu$. Then, for each $\xi\in L_\tau^2(\rho;{\mathbb R}^k)$, BSDE (equation BSDE1.1 of the paper) admits a unique weighted $L^2$ solution $(y_t,z_t)_{t\in[0,\tau]}$ in the space of $H_\tau^2(\rho;{\mathbb R}^{k}\times{\mathbb R}^{k\times d})$. Moreover, we have
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}\left[\int_0^{\tau}e^{2 \rho s}|y_s|^2{\rm d}s\right]<+\infty.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-09T07:38:10+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ebe1295e9102dd02623bcaa4a56cb21205f3f977868a5032865d9441b9b785d0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2.4 (Kac, Pleijel) of arXiv:2507.06186, '2507.06186'] If $\partial D$ is sufficiently regular (e.g., smooth), then
