           i\in \mathrm{Rec}(\sigma) \big).
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.669953+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee4b06394269e4ba6cbb657af731ec702cbec342313ed9775b92a2b04a6a07a4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 (Unmarked local limit) of arXiv:2608.04799, '2608.04799'] For every fixed \(q\ge1\), the factorial moment measures of
\(\mathcal X_n\) converge vaguely on \((0,\infty)^q\) to the measure with
density \(\overline m_\lambda^{(q)}\).  Moreover, for every
\(0<a<b<\infty\), there are \(C,c>0\) such that
\begin{equation}
  \E[(\mathcal X_n([a,b]))_q]\le C^q e^{-cq^3},
  \qquad q\ge1,\quad n\ge n_\lambda.
\end{equation}
