{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.531023+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5bbc97c66c1e5d0dde9b1d2cf67f7cf202f1e4955ba78e9369760c62ab193b6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 4 (No dichotomy in the Cauchy case) of arXiv:2608.30668, 'Recurrence and capacity of stable branching random walks'] When $\mu$ satisfies \Cref{Assum:Cauchy} and $\theta$ has finite moment of order $\delta$ for all $\delta >0$, then a
