{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.100291+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5fac8bbfcfa2a5dfa6f9688a8365046f268b6bfbeae7483d16bd883ae6d28e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:subcritical of arXiv:2601.20502, 'Optimal matching under size priority'] Define the families of truncated decorated trees $\left(\mathbb{T}_H,o,(i_{-}^{H},Z_{-}^H),(i_{+}^{H},Z_{+}^H)\right)_{H \geq 0}$ as follows:
    Sample $(\mathbb{T},o)$, set $\mathbb{T}_H=B_H(\mathbb{T},o)$ and   $(i_{-}^{H},Z_{-}^H)(u,v)=(0,0)$ for every edge of $\mathbb{T}_H$ pointing towards the $H-$boundary. Then use Recursion~(equation eq:systemrecursionzoombis of the paper) to define $(i_{-}^{H},Z_{-}^H)$ on the remainder of $\mathbb{T}_H$. We proceed similarly for $(i_{+}^{H},Z_{+}^H)$ by setting $(i_{+}^{H},Z_{+}^H)=(1,+\infty)$ on the boundary instead of $(0,0)$.

    Then under condition~(equation eq:subcriticalcond of the paper), both families $((i_{+}^{H},Z_{+}^H)(o,v))_{v \sim o}$ and $((i_{-}^{H},Z_{-}^H)(o,v))_{v \sim o}$ converge almost surely, as $H$ goes to infinity, to the same family $(i_l,Z_l)_{1 \leq l \leq N}$ where $(i_l,Z_l)$ have i.i.d distribution $\zeta'$ and are independent of $N \sim \pi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.686915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f61693da9163467538a99faf40147b50e3443aa1f63db92a28897646403f84d4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:poiss-approx of arXiv:2510.18856, 'Evolution of recursive trees with limited memory'] Let $D_{j,n}$ be the degree of vertex \textcolor{black}{$j$} at time $n$.
    For any $\epsilon > 1$, there exists $j_0$ such that for all $j_0 \leqslant j \leqslant n$,  \begin{align*}
        &d_{TV}\left(D_{j,n}, \text{Poisson}(1)\right) \\
        &\leqslant \epsilon \left[1-(1+\epsilon j^{\beta-1})^{-\beta}\right] + \epsilon j^{-\beta} + \max(\epsilon-1,j^{-\beta})+ \mathds{1}\left\{N_j\geqslant n-j\right\} \abs{\frac{n-j}{j^\beta}-1}
    \end{align*}where $N_j = \abs{\left\{i\geqslant j:i-i^\beta \leqslant j\right\}}.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:12.366015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f61b89d5abd13bee419c047fc9a0d682321a1ff676840e0932cb9a4baa2b0760","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random Hölder velocity fields' (problem environment).] Construct for some $d \in \N$, $\alpha > 1/2$ a single $u \in C^\alpha(\T^d)$ such that the ODE
