{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.530593+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f67ac4e25ed66cb896b921acb6caebf454894b2e5be355234acbabb4ffa88155","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 3 (Recurrence of BRW in low dimension) of arXiv:2608.30668, 'Recurrence and capacity of stable branching random walks'] Recall that \(\mu \in \mathrm{dom}(\alpha)\) for \(\alpha \in (1,2]\), and assume that $\theta$ has finite moment of order $\delta$ for all $\delta < \frac{2\alpha}{\alpha-1}$.
