{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.858446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6a33eb980ab1a9cdf2201a9fdc5dcbdba6b7da0a31237c49f09ff5745a93343","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:process_continuity of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] The process $X^a$ is almost surely continuous in the sense that
