{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.615901+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7265c90ec58f57f73fb503800b0df623e9db9d12fcda2416b991d89384775d9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Recall the definition of $a_n(t)$ from \eqref{E:1.24a}. There exist~$c,\tilde c >0$ such that
\begin{equation}

P^\varrho\Bigl(\,\max_{x\in\BbbL_n}\sqrt{L_t(x)}\ge\sqrt t+a_n(t)+u\Bigr)\le c(1+u)\texte^{-2\slb\, u-\tilde c u^2/n}
\end{equation}
holds for all $n\ge1$,  $t>0$ and all~$u>0$. Moreover, there exist~$c_1,c_2>0$ such that \begin{equation}

P^\varrho\biggl(\,\Bigl|\,\max_{x\in\BbbL_n}\sqrt{L_t(x)}-\sqrt t-a_n(t\vee1)\Bigr|>u\,\bigg|\,\max_{x\in\BbbL_n}L_t(x)>0\biggr)\le c_1\texte^{-c_2 u}
\end{equation}
holds for all~$n\ge1$, all $t>0$ and all $u\in(0,n]$.  Here $s\vee t:=\max\{s,t\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:25:49.869012+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f72d6d19ef785025ebab59b2ee12d380d26921fd8d62d715de5433a2ea78c66f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2609.02050, '2609.02050'] The Schur character $\chi_D({\bf x})$ is zero-one (attains the lower bound of \eqref{eq-ineq-x}) if and only if the valid part of $D$ satisfies one of the following conditions:		
