{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.328481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f788f8fecca6f9c172d364239eefdf4a7513f1cc593fd534f475e11ce3b6827f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem CAF of arXiv:2411.06571, 'Moment-based approach for two erratic KPZ scaling limits'] Let $\mathbf E_{\mathrm{BM}}^x$ denote expectation with respect to a standard Brownian motion on $\Bbb R$, started from $x\in\Bbb R$. There exists some universal constant $C>0$, such that uniformly over all smooth functions $\phi\ge 0$ with $\int_{\Bbb R} \phi =1,$ and all $s,t ,q\ge 0$, one has 
    \begin{align*}
        \sup_{x\in\Bbb R} \mathbf E^x_{\mathrm{BM}}\bigg[\bigg|\int_s^t \phi(B_s)ds\bigg|^q\bigg]^{1/q} &\leq Cq^{1/2} |t-s|^{1/2}\\
        \sup_{x\in\Bbb R} \mathbf E^x_{\mathrm{BM}}[e^{q \int_0^t \phi(B_s)ds}] &\leq Ce^{Cq^2 t}.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:01.830450+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f78e0e5bd9bf4943d83eaf674a2bfaf44c405e93b614a112aba8c62c5132c248","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:HS-curvature-full of arXiv:2609.00556, 'Higgs--Demailly System and Positivity of Higgs Bundles'] On a Riemann surface the Hitchin--Simpson curvature is of type $(1,1)$ and is
