  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:10.806784+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fec4edb3c85e71998e6781d82224b127c4173eafe9c5aaa7cd95da3fbe405513","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2512.19517, 'Spiking and Resetting'] Let $e^\varepsilon_2$ be the stopping time defined by 
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
e^\varepsilon_2 = \inf \{ t \ge e_1^\varepsilon \; ; \; X_t^\varepsilon =0 \} \ .
\end{split}
\end{equation}
We have that
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
\lim_{\varepsilon \to 0} \mathbb P (e^\varepsilon_2 > t)  = e^{f(1) t}  \ ,
\end{split}
\end{equation}
i.e. $(e^\varepsilon_2)_{\varepsilon>0}$ converges in law to an exponential random variable with parameter $-f(1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.989904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fee131587a418109488c3bdb9af7d327162f627a246c989c59cc046922122405","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Hada of arXiv:2509.02074, 'On the Kolmogorov-Feller weak law of large numbers for the Fr\'{e}chet mean on non-compact'] Suppose that $(M,d)$ is a Hadamard manifold. For any $x,x_1, x_2,\ldots,x_n \in M$, 
\begin{equation}
\|\mbox{Log}_{x}(\mu_{n}) \|_{x} \le  \|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mbox{Log}_{x}(x_i) \|_{x},
\end{equation}
where $\mu_{n}$ denotes the sample Fr\'{e}chet\ mean of $(x_1, x_2, \ldots x_n) \in M^n$, and $\|\cdot\|_{x}$ denotes the Riemannian norm induced by the Riemannian metric $\langle ~,~\rangle_{x}$ on $T_{x}M$. The inequality in ((ineq:key of the paper)) is strict unless $x,x_1,…,x_n$ all lie in a single totally geodesic flat submanifold of $M$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.705773+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fef4688b2456adb307b3e4429929556fc53266b2bc4289e84f489589d21499ee","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem derivative of arXiv:2609.00672, 'Deciding superellipticity and computing the Weierstrass normal form'] Let $D$ be one of the divisors $F_\infty$ and $nQ$, $Q$ a point of $S$, and put $S'=S$, respectively $S'=S-Q$. Then

